{"_id":"wmPlayerGuide001","name":"Wrathmaker — Player Guide","ownership":{"default":2},"pages":[{"_id":"wmGuidePage00001","name":"Welcome & quick reference","type":"text","sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Welcome &amp; quick reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Your central reference for Wrathmaker's additions to Pathfinder 2e. Use the journal's page list to jump to a topic. These are campaign house rules, not replacements for every PF2e rule.</p><p>The tables show the module's current defaults. Your character sheet, item and Workbench show your campaign's configured values; ask the GM if they differ. Optional features may not be enabled.</p><ul><li>Choose a profession on your character sheet; its feats appear under Profession Feats.</li><li>Track Hero Points on your character and Nephilim Points on the party.</li><li>Use the party Exploration tab for travel and the Workbench for crafting, gathering and disassembly.</li><li>Look under Pathfinder 2E Wrathmaker in Compendium Packs for the additional items, professions and guides.</li></ul><p>The Mark pages at the end include sources and descriptions. A listed Mark is a reference, not an automatic grant: your item and artisan must qualify.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00002","name":"Professions & specialisations","type":"text","sort":200000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Professions &amp; specialisations</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Choose one starting profession at level 1. It grants its named Lore and Additional Lore; it no longer grants Specialty Crafting or an extra profession-specific feat. Profession Feats are grouped beneath their parent profession.</p><p>Lore proficiency is trained at level 1, expert at 3, master at 7 and legendary at 15. At levels 4, 10 and 16, choose a specialty of your starting profession or learn a new profession. Specialty Lore follows the same proficiency progression.</p><p>Relevant profession checks receive a +2 circumstance bonus. This does not stack with another circumstance bonus on the same check. Each specialisation has Signature, Mastery and Legacy sections; use its current description, and do not treat unresolved placeholders as granted benefits.</p><h2>Blacksmithing</h2><ul><li><strong>Hellforging</strong>: Infernal weapons and armour shaped through fear, flame, sacrifice, and battle-tested tempers.</li><li><strong>Radiant Forging</strong>: Protective and cleansing equipment that channels light, healing, and defence of others.</li><li><strong>Azlanti Artifice</strong>: Ancient magitek, reverse-engineered machinery, original devices, and advanced infrastructure.</li></ul><h2>Alchemy</h2><ul><li><strong>Grand Apothecary</strong>: Refined potions and elixirs tailored for stability, duration, delivery, or specialised outcomes.</li><li><strong>Venomcraft</strong>: Custom toxins shaped around delivery, persistence, concealment, onset, or a chosen quarry.</li><li><strong>Transmutative Alchemy</strong>: Controlled material conversion and the creation of specialist composite substances.</li></ul><h2>Enchanting</h2><ul><li><strong>Aethercasting</strong>: Controlled magical enhancements and the incremental upgrading of empowered items.</li><li><strong>Essencebinding</strong>: Approved item traits and harvested essences bound safely into qualifying equipment.</li><li><strong>Runecarving</strong>: Efficient rune creation, upgrading, transfer, and linked Rune Echoes.</li></ul><h2>Leatherwork</h2><ul><li><strong>Wyrmcraft</strong>: Dragon-scale equipment that preserves an adaptation belonging to the source dragon.</li><li><strong>Beastbinding</strong>: Prepared hides that preserve a useful natural quality of the creature they came from.</li><li><strong>Mantlecraft</strong>: Prestigious and protective mantles, cloaks, robes, and environmental garments.</li></ul><h2>Carpentry</h2><ul><li><strong>Warbowyer</strong>: Engineered bows, crossbows, ballistae, loading systems, and specialist ammunition.</li><li><strong>Masterwright</strong>: Bridges, roads, docks, fieldworks, buildings, and major wooden structures.</li><li><strong>Warcarving</strong>: Combat forms and utility carvings applied to wooden weapons, shields, and tools.</li></ul><h2>Stonemasonry</h2><ul><li><strong>Megalithics</strong>: Monumental works, fortresses, roads, aqueducts, walls, and major civil structures.</li><li><strong>Runemasonry</strong>: Wardstones and enduring magical inscriptions that protect places rather than carried items.</li><li><strong>Titanmasonry</strong>: Stone wargear, constructs, siege engines, and powerful Titanic forms.</li></ul><h2>Glassmaking</h2><ul><li><strong>Prismcraft</strong>: Lenses and prisms that focus, split, redirect, or transform light and magical energy.</li><li><strong>Mirrorcraft</strong>: Reflective magic, illusions, scrying, communication, and linked mirrors.</li><li><strong>Aetherglass</strong>: Mana batteries, spell reservoirs, magical circuitry, construct cores, and powered components.</li></ul><h2>Pottery</h2><ul><li><strong>Ceramancy</strong>: Living clay, terracotta constructs, ceramic armour, figurines, and guardians.</li><li><strong>Reliquarycraft</strong>: Vessels that preserve blessings, curses, spirits, essences, and planar energy.</li><li><strong>Pyroceramics</strong>: Crucibles, bomb casings, heat-resistant vessels, magical kilns, and industrial ceramics.</li></ul><h2>Weaving</h2><ul><li><strong>Aetherweaving</strong>: Manathread and magical cloth that carry enchantments, wards, and arcane patterns.</li><li><strong>Ironweaving</strong>: Warcloth, armour backing, nets, ropes, bowstrings, sails, and resilient reinforcement.</li><li><strong>Heraldweaving</strong>: Standards, banners, and tapestries supporting morale, identity, armies, and prestige.</li></ul><h2>Bookmaking</h2><ul><li><strong>Grimoirecraft</strong>: Living spellbooks and codices with enhanced memory, resonance, organisation, and access.</li><li><strong>Chroniclecraft</strong>: Lore, formulae, techniques, and Codices of Mastery that make recorded knowledge usable.</li><li><strong>Grand Cartography</strong>: Master atlases for exploration, resources, roads, armies, settlements, and expansion.</li></ul><h2>Tailoring</h2><ul><li><strong>Battlestitching</strong>: Combat garments and armour liners designed for movement, access, protection, and adaptation.</li><li><strong>Veilcraft</strong>: Supernatural disguises, stealth clothing, concealing mantles, and perception-altering garments.</li><li><strong>Regaliacraft</strong>: Vestments of authority supporting diplomacy, leadership, morale, royal courts, and prestige.</li></ul></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00003","name":"Hero & Nephilim Points","type":"text","sort":300000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Hero &amp; Nephilim Points</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><h2>Hero Points</h2><p>You can hold up to 10 Hero Points. Unspent points carry over between sessions. Use the normal character-sheet control; ordinary Hero Point spending rules still apply unless your GM says otherwise.</p><h2>Nephilim Points</h2><p>The party has a separate shared tracker from 0 to 10 in its header. These points persist with the party. Wrathmaker tracks the total but does not define automatic powers or spending benefits; your GM explains when they are earned or spent.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00004","name":"Equipment, Core materials & Apex items","type":"text","sort":400000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Equipment, Core materials &amp; Apex items</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>A crafted item combines a PF2e base item, a Core material and optional Artisan Marks. Core progression replaces rune-style progression on that item; do not add the replaced rune benefits a second time.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Weapon attack</th><th>Extra damage dice</th><th>Spell attack / DC</th><th>Armor AC / saves</th><th>Capacity</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>+0</td><td>0</td><td>+0</td><td>+0 / +0</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>+1</td><td>1</td><td>+1</td><td>+1 / +1</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>+2</td><td>2</td><td>+2</td><td>+2 / +2</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>+3</td><td>2</td><td>+3</td><td>+3 / +3</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>+4</td><td>3</td><td>+4</td><td>+4 / +4</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>+5</td><td>4</td><td>+5</td><td>+5 / +5</td><td>8</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Weapon dice are additional dice, not flat damage. Shields gain +3 Hardness and +30 HP per Core progression step. The displayed item includes applicable modifications.</p><h2>Spell Focus</h2><p>A held Metal or Wood focus grants its Core spellcasting bonus to spell attacks and DCs, not spell damage, slots or proficiency. Only the strongest held focus applies.</p><h2>Dragon Scales</h2><p>Scales enhance Metal or Leather/Hide armor. Hatchling, Juvenile, Youth, Adult, Ancient and Arch Dragon grant default resistance values 1, 4, 8, 12, 16 and 20. Black grants acid, Blue electricity, Green poison, Red fire and White cold resistance while the armor is equipped.</p><h2>Apex ability equipment</h2><p>Wrathmaker's 30 worn items grant +1 to +5 to Strength, Dexterity, Constitution, Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma. Wear and invest the item, then use its circled A on the character sheet. Different attributes can be active together; for the same attribute only the strongest applies. Belts, rings, amulets, circlets, sashes and brooches form the collection. These are campaign rewards, not a priced shop list.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00005","name":"Resource catalogue","type":"text","sort":500000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Resource catalogue</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Resources are Equipment with the Precious tag. Each inventory unit is one Resource Unit, including named lots of crystals or scales. Five units weigh 1 Bulk; ten weigh 2 Bulk. Prices below are full unit values, before a sale discount. Existing older inventory copies may still appear as Treasure.</p><p>Tier levels are 1, 4, 8, 12, 16 and 20, with default level-based DCs 15, 19, 24, 30, 35 and 40. The actual attempt may have an adjustment.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Resource</th><th>Tier</th><th>Level</th><th>Unit value</th><th>Unit Bulk</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Iron Ingot</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Steel Ingot</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Cold Iron Ingot</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Mithril Ingot</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Adamantium Ingot</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Dark Iron Ingot</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Softwood Lumber</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Hardwood Lumber</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Blackwood Lumber</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Darkmoon Lumber</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Starwood Lumber</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Godwood Lumber</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Fieldstone Block</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Granite Block</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Obsidian Block</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Runestone Block</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Celestite Block</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Worldstone Block</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Rawhide Sheet</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Hardened Leather Sheet</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Ironhide Sheet</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Moonhide Sheet</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Titanhide Sheet</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Primordial Hide Sheet</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Greenleaf Bundle</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Embercap Bundle</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Ghostmoss Bundle</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Moonbloom Bundle</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Starspore Bundle</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Worldroot Bundle</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Faint Mana Crystals (10)</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Charged Mana Crystals (10)</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Resonant Mana Crystals (10)</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Arcane Prisms (10)</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Astral Crystals (10)</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Aetherheart Crystals (10)</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Hatchling Black Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>4.5 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Juvenile Black Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>22.5 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Youth Black Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>127.5 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Adult Black Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>525 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Ancient Black Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>2400 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Arch Dragon Black Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>16500 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Hatchling Blue Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>4.5 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Juvenile Blue Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>22.5 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Youth Blue Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>127.5 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Adult Blue Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>525 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Ancient Blue Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>2400 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Arch Dragon Blue Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>16500 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Hatchling Green Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>4.5 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Juvenile Green Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>22.5 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Youth Green Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>127.5 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Adult Green Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>525 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Ancient Green Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>2400 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Arch Dragon Green Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>16500 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Hatchling Red Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>4.5 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Juvenile Red Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>22.5 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Youth Red Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>127.5 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Adult Red Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>525 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Ancient Red Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>2400 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Arch Dragon Red Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>16500 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Hatchling White Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>4.5 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Juvenile White Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>22.5 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Youth White Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>127.5 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Adult White Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>525 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Ancient White Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>2400 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Arch Dragon White Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>16500 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr></tbody></table></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00006","name":"Crafting in the Workbench","type":"text","sort":600000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Crafting in the Workbench</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><ol><li>Choose the party, drop a supported base item into Craft, and select its recipe, Core material and Tier.</li><li>Add one lead artisan. Every supported recipe can be crafted solo. Additional material specialists unlock their eligible Marks and combinations rather than access to the base item.</li><li>Choose Marks and compatible Anchors. Review materials, Capacity and required progress.</li><li>Create the project to reserve Party Stash stock. Reservations prevent promising the same stock to multiple projects; they do not consume it.</li><li>Commit downtime and resolve Work Blocks. At completion, review and confirm the resource consumption and finished item.</li></ol><h2>Working together</h2><p>Up to six distinct artisans contribute. Each spends the same calendar downtime. Teamwork work rates are ×1 for 1–2 artisans, ×1.25 for 3–5, and ×1.5 for six. Fractional Progress carries between blocks. For a block of D days (1–5), the base success gives D Progress; critical success gives ceiling(1.5 × D); failure gives zero for one day or floor(D ÷ 2) for longer blocks; critical failure gives zero. Apply the teamwork rate to that base Progress. Time estimates assume success.</p><p>Cancel a project to release unspent reservations. Archive finished projects to keep the list manageable. Deleting a record does not refund spent materials. Report a missing finished item to the GM rather than crafting a duplicate.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00007","name":"Artisan Marks & activations","type":"text","sort":700000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Artisan Marks &amp; activations</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Click an artisan to choose Marks. Sources identify the profession and specialisation. Item compatibility, Anchors, minimum Tiers, stock and stacking rules still apply; extra artisans do not automatically activate every synergy.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Grade</th><th>Capacity cost</th><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Minor</td><td>0</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Standard</td><td>1</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Major</td><td>2</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>Superior</td><td>3</td><td>4</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Mark is allowed per item. Capacity is shared across all artisans. Secondary structural material must normally be at least Core Tier minus two. Some Marks impose stricter requirements.</p><p>Make & Marks on the finished item records the Core, applied Marks and makers. Chat badges provide compact provenance. Structure-only and consumable-only Marks do not appear in the equipment picker.</p><p>Some numerical effects are automated, others require their condition to be selected or resolved during play. For explicit action costs, Add Mark Actions to Wielder creates native action entries on the owning character. These post the rules; they do not automatically resolve targets, damage or limited uses. An unspecified action cost is not permission to activate for free. Remove a linked action when its item is lost or transferred.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00008","name":"Gathering, upgrades & disassembly","type":"text","sort":800000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Gathering, upgrades &amp; disassembly</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><h2>Gather</h2><p>Use the Workbench Gather tab. Select a character, environment and resource; review its Tier, skill, DC, time and expected yield, then attempt the check. Region and environment can restrict available goods. Rewards go to the party or gathering character according to your campaign settings.</p><h2>Upgrade</h2><p>Stow and uninvest a single crafted item, then drop it into Upgrade. Choose a new Core material or Tier, secondary materials and Tiers, or dragon scales. Existing Marks and their makers remain; incompatible anchors block the upgrade. One existing Mark can move to a compatible anchor for free. New Marks use normal capacity, materials and work.</p><p>Replacement components require 25% fewer materials, rounded up per requirement, and 25% less component work. Unchanged components cost nothing. Old replaced materials are lost. Reservations and artisan teamwork follow normal projects; completion consumes the replacements and updates the original item, not a copy. Cancel to release the item and resources. Reserved items cannot be edited, equipped or dismantled. Use the latest project for recovery or disassembly.</p><p>Dragon-scale Resource Units cost 1.5 times the normal tier value. Mana crystals use normal tier prices.</p><h2>Disassemble</h2><p>Drop a Wrathmaker-formatted item from your sheet or Party Stash into Disassemble. Review returns before confirming: the item is destroyed. Default recovery is 50%, rounded up separately for each material, Tier and variant. Recorded items use their project ledger; other compatible items show a standard-recipe estimate. Returns go to the selected Party Stash. Dismantled items cannot be salvaged twice or recovered as missing outputs.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00009","name":"Flanking","type":"text","sort":900000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Flanking</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>First establish a normal opposite-side flank with two qualifying melee combatants in reach. Additional qualifying combatants can contribute from other sides.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Qualifying combatants</th><th>Final target AC penalty</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>2</td><td>−2: Off-guard (Flanked)</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>−3: Outnumbered (Flanked)</td></tr><tr><td>4 or more</td><td>−4: Surrounded (Flanked)</td></tr></tbody></table><p>These are final penalties, not additions to the normal −2. Only qualifying melee attacks benefit; ranged attacks do not inherit this flanking penalty. Reach weapons count when they can reach the target. A creature unable to flank or an immune target follows its normal restrictions.</p><p>If the target is more than one size category larger than the largest qualifying flanker, the enhanced thresholds become six for −3 and eight for −4. A normal two-person flank still gives −2.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00010","name":"Party travel & exploration","type":"text","sort":1000000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Party travel &amp; exploration</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>The party's Exploration tab combines normal exploration activities with travel setup, rider assignments and the daily plan. On foot, the slowest member limits shared Speed. Vehicle riders use transport Speed, while walkers can still slow the group. Pulled transport uses the slowest selected hauler, subject to the vehicle limit.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Shared Speed</th><th>Activities per day</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>10 feet or less</td><td>½ (one activity over two days)</td></tr><tr><td>15–25 feet</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>30–40 feet</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>45–55 feet</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>60 feet or more</td><td>4</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Assign Travel, Reconnoiter, Fortify Camp, Map the Area, Subsist or Other and mark activities Used as they finish. Save Travel Plan preserves choices; Begin Day & Share posts the plan. The sun button starts a new day.</p><h2>Express Rider house rule</h2><p>Select the character rolling Nature, pulling creatures and up to six affected party travellers, including walkers. The check uses the highest selected Will DC. Success or critical success increases affected overland Speeds by half for that day. Unaffected walkers and vehicle limits still constrain the group. This changes overland travel, not encounter Speed.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00011","name":"Blacksmithing — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1100000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Blacksmithing — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>High-power campaign revision: all 253 Marks have been reviewed. Flat Artisan bonuses stack; resistances use the highest applicable source. Capacity and the one-free-Mark limit still apply.</p><p>Campaign descriptions are not a promise that every effect is automated. Supported passive numbers use the item rules; activations, auras, project changes and special riders require manual resolution unless stated otherwise. Native action readouts do not spend uses automatically. Structure Marks never grant character bonuses.</p><p>Where a Mark grants a separate 10-point temporary-HP buffer, track it alongside class temporary HP. Spend the Artisan buffer first, then ordinary temporary HP, then HP. Different Mark buffers may coexist; the same grant cannot refill through re-equipping and expires as written. Maximum-HP increases are not healing.</p><h2>Universal Artisan Marks</h2><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-universal-tempered-construction\"><h4>Tempered Construction</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Armor or shield gains +50% of its pre-Mark maximum item HP and +Core Tier Hardness. This improves the item, not its wearer&#39;s HP. Durability bonuses add against the same pre-Mark base; they do not multiply each other.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-universal-perfect-balance\"><h4>Perfect Balance</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Weapon grants an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to one chosen Athletics manoeuvre made using it. Enable the Mark condition only while using this weapon for that manoeuvre. No Bulk reduction.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-universal-reinforced-edge\"><h4>Reinforced Edge</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · 2 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Weapon deals +3 damage per weapon damage die against objects. At Core Tier 5+, this becomes +5 per die. Enable the object-target toggle; this does not ignore Hardness. Sundering Drive — Two actions, once per encounter: make one Strike with this weapon against an object. On a hit, add 3 × Core Tier damage before Hardness. This Strike counts toward multiple attack penalty normally; the additional damage is resolved manually.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 1 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-universal-fortified-frame\"><h4>Fortified Frame</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Armor or shield has ×2 pre-Mark maximum item HP at Core Tiers 1–3, ×3 at Tiers 4–5, and ×4 at Tier 6, plus 2 × Core Tier Hardness. Other durability bonuses add against the same pre-Mark base, not this multiplied value. This does not grant wearer HP or AC.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 1 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-universal-master-reforge\"><h4>Master Reforge</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Project</p><p>Rebuilding recovers 90% of recorded ordinary components, rounded down, and preserves compatible Marks. Recovered value cannot exceed actual inputs; no duplicated items or components. Unique resources require GM approval.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 1 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article></div><h2>Hellforging</h2><p>Infernal weapons and armour shaped through fear, flame, sacrifice, and battle-tested tempers.</p><h3>Signature — Infernal Temper</h3><p>Create Hellforged equipment built around fire, blood, fear, retaliation and dangerous power.</p><h3>Mastery — Furnace Without Mercy</h3><p>Reduce Hellforging special-resource cost by 20%; at high tier recover 50% of rare infernal components from dismantled Hellforged gear.</p><h3>Legacy — Infernal Foundry</h3><p>Supports elite army weapons, infernal siege ammunition and intimidating military infrastructure.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-1-ember-temper\"><h4>Ember Temper</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Weapon sheds controllable light and deals additional fire damage equal to 4 × Core Tier on a critical hit only.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Hellforging · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-1-blood-temper\"><h4>Blood Temper</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>While the wielder is at or below half maximum HP, this weapon deals +4 × Core Tier damage. This is the wielder&#39;s HP, not the target&#39;s.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Hellforging · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 1 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-1-hellfire-channel\"><h4>Hellfire Channel</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · 1 Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Once per encounter, ignite the weapon for 1 minute. Its Strikes deal additional Core Tier d8 fire damage. Fire resistance is reduced by 3 × Core Tier against this added damage only, minimum 0; immunity is unaffected.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Hellforging · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 1 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-1-tormentors-edge\"><h4>Tormentor&#39;s Edge</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Free Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Once per round after this weapon critically hits, the target attempts a Will save against your higher class or spell DC. Failure: frightened 2; critical failure: frightened 3 and fleeing until the end of its next turn. Success: no effect. This is a mental, fear effect.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Hellforging · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 1 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-1-perfected-killing-edge\"><h4>Executioner&#39;s Ember</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>A weapon deals additional precision damage equal to Core Tier d8 against a creature at or below half maximum HP. Enable the Mark condition only against an eligible target. Precision immunity applies.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Hellforging · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 2 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-1-soul-burned-steel\"><h4>Soul-Burned Steel</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Reaction</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Reaction, once per day when damage would reduce you to 0 HP without killing you outright: remain at 1 HP, Step up to 15 feet and make one Strike with this weapon. Afterwards gain drained 1 until daily preparations. It does not prevent death effects.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Hellforging · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 2 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article></div><h2>Radiant Forging</h2><p>Protective and cleansing equipment that channels light, healing, and defence of others.</p><h3>Signature — Radiant Temper</h3><p>Create protective, cleansing and celestial equipment, especially effective against undead, fiends and corruption.</p><h3>Mastery — Purified Forge</h3><p>Reduce sacred/celestial resource waste by 20% and improve repairs to Radiant equipment.</p><h3>Legacy — Beacon Works</h3><p>Supports hospitals, temples, settlement wards, anti-undead defences and sacred military equipment.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-2-consecrated-finish\"><h4>Consecrated Finish</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>While worn or wielded, gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Religion checks to Recall Knowledge about undead or fiends. Enable the Mark condition for an eligible subject. The item bears a visible sacred dedication; it does not automatically bypass sanctification requirements.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-2-dawnbound\"><h4>Dawnbound</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Weapon deals +3 spirit damage per weapon damage die against undead and fiends. Other targets gain no added damage.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 1 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-2-guardians-radiance\"><h4>Guardian&#39;s Radiance</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Reaction</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Reaction, once per round when an ally within 15 feet takes damage: reduce that instance by 6 × Core Tier, minimum 0. Requires the item worn or wielded; does not redirect damage to you.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 1 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-2-aegis-of-dawn\"><h4>Aegis of Dawn</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants +12 × Core Tier maximum HP and spirit and void resistance equal to 3 × Core Tier. This is maximum HP, not temporary HP or healing; repeated equipping must not restore damage.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 1 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-2-martyrs-forge\"><h4>Martyr&#39;s Forge</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Reaction</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Reaction, once per encounter when an ally within 30 feet takes damage: take unpreventable damage equal to your level and reduce the ally&#39;s instance by 8 × your level, minimum 0. You cannot use this if the sacrifice would reduce you to 0 HP.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 2 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-2-solar-ascension\"><h4>Solar Ascension</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 2 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Two actions, once per day: for 1 minute radiate bright light in a 30-foot aura. Allies including you gain +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to AC and saves while inside. Undead and fiends starting their turns inside take 3 × Core Tier d6 spirit damage, basic Will save against your higher class or spell DC.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 2 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article></div><h2>Azlanti Artifice</h2><p>Ancient magitek, reverse-engineered machinery, original devices, and advanced infrastructure.</p><h3>Signature — Lost Artifice</h3><p>Reverse-engineer ancient technology, repair magitek and invent designs beyond normal PF2e equipment lists.</p><h3>Mastery — Reverse Engineering</h3><p>Preserve the original device while producing a reusable blueprint; repeat builds take 25% less downtime.</p><h3>Legacy — Arcane Industrialisation</h3><p>Enables automated workshops, magical power, transport, constructs and advanced siege technology.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-3-diagnostic-matrix\"><h4>Diagnostic Matrix</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>While wielded or worn, gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Crafting checks to Repair or Identify Magic involving this item&#39;s mechanism. Enable the Mark condition only when this item is the subject; its display also reports damage.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-3-integrated-conduit\"><h4>Integrated Conduit</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Project</p><p>The item can accommodate two additional Mana or Aetherglass component sockets without added Bulk. Supply their materials normally. Sockets do not grant free Marks, Capacity, or Core progression.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 1 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-3-adaptive-configuration\"><h4>Adaptive Configuration</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · 1 Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Choose three legal weapon damage types or tool configurations at creation. One Interact action switches the active mode. Only one mode applies at a time; it cannot grant extra Marks or combine incompatible weapon statistics.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 1 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-3-arcane-mechanism\"><h4>Arcane Mechanism</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · 2 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Two actions, once per encounter: emit a 30-foot line dealing 2 × Core Tier d8 electricity damage with a basic Reflex save against your higher class or spell DC. Mechanism must be wielded. This is an electricity and magical effect.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 1 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-3-phase-mechanism\"><h4>Phase Mechanism</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 1 Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>One action, once per encounter: Stride up to your Speed through creatures and up to 10 feet of non-magical solid obstacles. End in an open space you can perceive; if none is reachable, the action fails without moving. This is magical movement, not teleportation.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 2 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-3-reality-engine\"><h4>Reality Engine</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 1 Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>One action, once per day: for 1 minute, once on each of your turns reduce one two-action activation of this item&#39;s other Marks to one action. Cannot reduce spellcasting, reactions, free actions, or this activation; does not refresh uses or bypass prerequisites.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 2 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article></div></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00012","name":"Alchemy — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1200000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Alchemy — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>High-power campaign revision: all 253 Marks have been reviewed. Flat Artisan bonuses stack; resistances use the highest applicable source. Capacity and the one-free-Mark limit still apply.</p><p>Campaign descriptions are not a promise that every effect is automated. Supported passive numbers use the item rules; activations, auras, project changes and special riders require manual resolution unless stated otherwise. Native action readouts do not spend uses automatically. Structure Marks never grant character bonuses.</p><p>Where a Mark grants a separate 10-point temporary-HP buffer, track it alongside class temporary HP. Spend the Artisan buffer first, then ordinary temporary HP, then HP. Different Mark buffers may coexist; the same grant cannot refill through re-equipping and expires as written. Maximum-HP increases are not healing.</p><h2>Universal Artisan Marks</h2><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-universal-stable-formula\"><h4>Stable Formula</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Consumable</p><p>A dose lasts four times its normal shelf life and resists mundane temperature spoilage while sealed. This does not extend its effect duration or preserve an opened dose indefinitely.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-universal-efficient-batch\"><h4>Efficient Batch</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Project</p><p>A batch produces 25% additional identical doses, rounded down, minimum one extra per four paid doses. Bonus doses are outputs, not additional inputs for applying this Mark again.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-universal-refined-reagent\"><h4>Refined Reagent</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Consumable</p><p>Choose one fixed healing, movement-distance or resistance value at creation; multiply that value by 2 when the dose is used. Do not multiply DCs, damage, action counts, condition values, or resource returns.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 1 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-universal-quick-preparation\"><h4>Quick Preparation</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Project</p><p>Reduce this batch&#39;s required artisan-days by 40%, rounded up to whole days with a minimum of one. Apply to the original duration, not repeatedly to previously reduced work.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 1 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-universal-catalyst-reserve\"><h4>Catalyst Reserve</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Project</p><p>Reduce one named secondary ordinary resource cost by 25%, rounded down, minimum one unit still required. It cannot reduce Core, unique ingredients or its own catalyst cost.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 1 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article></div><h2>Grand Apothecary</h2><p>Refined potions and elixirs tailored for stability, duration, delivery, or specialised outcomes.</p><h3>Signature — Refined Formula</h3><p>Customise medicines, potions and elixirs for potency, duration, administration and recovery.</p><h3>Mastery — Batch Distillation</h3><p>Produce 25% more doses from the same material input.</p><h3>Legacy — Royal Apothecary</h3><p>Supports hospitals, military medicine, plague response and settlement recovery.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-1-measured-dose\"><h4>Measured Dose</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Consumable</p><p>Halve one fixed numerical drawback of this dose, rounding its magnitude down. Cannot remove addiction, death, ability loss, action costs or a drawback that defines the item&#39;s identity.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Grand Apothecary · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-1-concentrated\"><h4>Concentrated</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Consumable</p><p>Multiply this dose&#39;s HP healing by 3. If it grants temporary HP instead, add only 10 temporary HP to a separately tracked Artisan buffer; never multiply the original temporary HP. The buffer expires with the dose and cannot be refreshed by re-equipping.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Grand Apothecary · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 1 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-1-extended-formula\"><h4>Extended Formula</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Consumable</p><p>An effect lasting at least 1 minute lasts four times as long, maximum 24 hours. Does not extend persistent damage, poison stages, resource regeneration or another Mark&#39;s effect.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Grand Apothecary · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 1 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-1-rapid-infusion\"><h4>Rapid Infusion</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · 1 Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Consumable</p><p>One action: draw this accessible dose and consume or administer it to a willing adjacent creature. No extra Interact action is required. A dose is still consumed; this does not make an unwilling target willing.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Grand Apothecary · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 1 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-1-restorative-panacea\"><h4>Restorative Panacea</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 1 Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Consumable</p><p>On consumption, restore 8 × Core Tier additional HP and reduce two of clumsy, enfeebled, frightened, sickened or stupefied by 2, minimum 0. Attempt one counteract check against poison or disease using the drinker&#39;s higher class/spell DC minus 10 and counteract rank equal to Core Tier. Ongoing sources can reapply conditions.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Grand Apothecary · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 2 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-1-phoenix-draught\"><h4>Phoenix Draught</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 1 Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Consumable</p><p>One action to drink. Once per day per creature, for 1 hour: the first damage that would reduce you to 0 HP without outright death instead leaves you at 1 HP and restores 10 × Core Tier HP. The draught then ends. It cannot prevent death effects or be chained with another Phoenix Draught.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Grand Apothecary · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 2 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article></div><h2>Venomcraft</h2><p>Custom toxins shaped around delivery, persistence, concealment, onset, or a chosen quarry.</p><h3>Signature — Toxin Refinement</h3><p>Customise poisons by delivery, onset, target profile, stages and concealment.</p><h3>Mastery — Venom Harvesting</h3><p>Gain 25% more usable poison material from venomous creatures and reduce poison resource cost by 15%.</p><h3>Legacy — Master Toxicologist</h3><p>Supports antivenom, pest control, military toxins and intelligence operations.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-2-masked-toxin\"><h4>Masked Toxin</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Consumable</p><p>The DC to detect this poison before exposure increases by Core Tier + 2. Its saving throw DC is unchanged; an identified poison remains identified.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Venomcraft · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-2-adhesive-poison\"><h4>Adhesive Poison</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Consumable</p><p>An applied injury poison survives misses and affects the next two successful weapon hits before the end of the encounter. Each hit follows normal exposure rules; hitting one creature twice does not create two independent copies of the same affliction.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Venomcraft · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 1 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-2-swift-venom\"><h4>Swift Venom</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Consumable</p><p>The poison&#39;s onset is immediate. On an initial failed save apply stage 1 immediately; on a critical failure apply stage 2 if available. Subsequent intervals are unchanged. A poison already having immediate onset gains +Core Tier to its initial save DC only.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Venomcraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 1 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-2-predator-formula\"><h4>Predator Formula</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Consumable</p><p>Choose one creature trait such as dragon, fiend or undead at creation. The poison gains +Core Tier + 2 to its save DC against that trait. This does not bypass poison immunity.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Venomcraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 1 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-2-mutagenic-venom\"><h4>Mutagenic Venom</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Consumable</p><p>Choose clumsy, enfeebled or stupefied at creation. When the poison reaches stage 3, apply the chosen condition at 3 for 1 round. The rider triggers at most once per round per creature and does not permanently change its stage.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Venomcraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 2 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-2-perfect-killer\"><h4>Perfect Killer</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Consumable</p><p>Poison save DC increases by 5. Once per target per dose, treat the first ordinary success as a failure; critical successes are unchanged. Poison immunity still applies, and the dose cannot retrigger this benefit via transfer.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Venomcraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 2 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article></div><h2>Transmutative Alchemy</h2><p>Controlled material conversion and the creation of specialist composite substances.</p><h3>Signature — Material Transmutation</h3><p>Convert resource families and create composite materials for other artisans.</p><h3>Mastery — The Great Work</h3><p>Standard conversion is 2 units into 1 equal-tier unit; mastered high-tier conversions can improve to 3 into 2.</p><h3>Legacy — Transmutation Industry</h3><p>Converts surplus Kingdom resources and enables specialised industrial projects.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-3-purified-matrix\"><h4>Purified Matrix</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Project</p><p>Remove up to three mundane impurities from a component without losing material quantity. Cannot remove curses, change rarity or erase an intrinsic hazardous magical property.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-3-alchemical-alloy\"><h4>Alchemical Alloy</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Project</p><p>Combine two paid same-tier material families into one component with both native tags. Choose one family for numerical Core progression; never add both Core progressions together.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 1 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-3-composite-matrix\"><h4>Composite Matrix</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Project</p><p>One composite component can satisfy two compatible family requirements. Pay both quantities and use the lower tier for eligibility; the benefit is sharing one socket, not free materials.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 1 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-3-refined-substance\"><h4>Refined Substance</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Project</p><p>For one named Mark&#39;s Anchor eligibility only, treat this component as two tiers higher, maximum 6. Its actual tier, Core progression, sale value and other Marks are unchanged.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 1 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-3-philosophers-matrix\"><h4>Philosopher&#39;s Matrix</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Project</p><p>Once per project replace up to two missing ordinary resource families with equal quantities of paid same-tier resources. Cannot substitute unique, dragon-origin or story-gated ingredients.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 2 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-3-living-transmutation\"><h4>Living Transmutation</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Project</p><p>Create three paid, compatible material identities for this component. Choose one during daily preparations. Native tags and eligibility change, but existing Marks must remain legal and only one identity supplies Core statistics.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 2 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article></div></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00013","name":"Enchanting — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1300000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Enchanting — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>High-power campaign revision: all 253 Marks have been reviewed. Flat Artisan bonuses stack; resistances use the highest applicable source. Capacity and the one-free-Mark limit still apply.</p><p>Campaign descriptions are not a promise that every effect is automated. Supported passive numbers use the item rules; activations, auras, project changes and special riders require manual resolution unless stated otherwise. Native action readouts do not spend uses automatically. Structure Marks never grant character bonuses.</p><p>Where a Mark grants a separate 10-point temporary-HP buffer, track it alongside class temporary HP. Spend the Artisan buffer first, then ordinary temporary HP, then HP. Different Mark buffers may coexist; the same grant cannot refill through re-equipping and expires as written. Maximum-HP increases are not healing.</p><h2>Universal Artisan Marks</h2><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-universal-stable-matrix\"><h4>Stable Matrix</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · 2 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>The item gains +Core Tier + 2 to its DC against counteract attempts targeting its magic. This protects the item only, not the bearer&#39;s spells, and does not make it immune to suppression. Spellbreak Guard — Two actions, once per encounter: gain +5 Artisan Bonus to your next saving throw against a spell before the start of your next turn. Wield or wear the item throughout. This does not counteract the spell and must be applied manually to that save.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-universal-attuned-craft\"><h4>Attuned Craft</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>During daily preparations authorise up to six named bearers to use this item&#39;s custom activations. An unauthorised user cannot activate them; it remains usable as an ordinary item. No effect on native spellcasting or ownership.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-universal-resonant-channel\"><h4>Resonant Channel</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Add two charges to one explicitly identified custom daily charge pool on this item. These charges return only at daily preparations; they cannot fuel charge-regeneration or Mark-refresh effects.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 1 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-universal-efficient-activation\"><h4>Efficient Activation</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Free Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Free action, once per encounter immediately before using this item&#39;s two-action custom activation: reduce it to one action. Cannot affect spellcasting, change use limits or combine with another action reduction on the same activation.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 1 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-universal-arcane-safeguard\"><h4>Arcane Safeguard</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Reduce self-damage from this item&#39;s own overload or critical activation failure by 75%, rounding damage down. Other creatures and normal enemy attacks are unaffected. Non-damage drawbacks remain.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 1 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article></div><h2>Aethercasting</h2><p>Controlled magical enhancements and the incremental upgrading of empowered items.</p><h3>Signature — Empowerment</h3><p>Create statistic-enhancing and magically sustained equipment that can intentionally push beyond ordinary PF2e ceilings.</p><h3>Mastery — Aether Refinement</h3><p>Upgrade an existing Empowerment by paying only the material difference and half normal upgrade downtime.</p><h3>Legacy — Permanent Enchantment</h3><p>Supports wards, magical utilities, powered workshops and settlement infrastructure.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-1-minor-empowerment\"><h4>Minor Empowerment</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Gain an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to one chosen narrow skill use. Enable the Mark condition only for the agreed use, not all checks with that skill.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Aethercasting · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-1-focused-empowerment\"><h4>Focused Empowerment</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Gain an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier to one selected skill or initiative while this item is wielded or worn.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Aethercasting · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 1 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-1-twin-empowerment\"><h4>Twin Empowerment</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Choose two different skills at creation. While wielded or worn gain +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to checks with both. Record the choices on the item; neither can be an attack, AC or spell DC.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Aethercasting · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 1 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-1-overcharged-matrix\"><h4>Overcharged Matrix</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Free Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Free action, once per encounter before one roll: add 5 to one existing positive flat Artisan bonus on this item for that roll only. Cannot improve Over-Potency, a multiplier, DC, condition, resource quantity or another Overcharged Matrix. This cannot raise the +2 per-Mark Over-Potency cap.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Aethercasting · Core Tier 3+; Core-tier Anchor required</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 1 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-1-overlord-matrix\"><h4>Overlord Matrix</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>While wielded or held, weapon gains +2 Artisan Bonus to its attack rolls, or spell focus gains +2 Artisan Bonus to spell attack and spell DC. This Over-Potency is capped at +2 per Mark beyond Core progression and stacks with different Marks.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Aethercasting · Core Tier 4+; Core-tier Anchor required</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 2 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-1-aetherheart-lattice\"><h4>Aetherheart Lattice</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 1 Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>One action, three charges per day: refresh one expended once-per-encounter Standard or Major activation on this item. Each target activation can be refreshed once per day. Cannot refresh charges, healing, recovery, action-reduction or other refresh effects.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Aethercasting · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 2 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article></div><h2>Essencebinding</h2><p>Approved item traits and harvested essences bound safely into qualifying equipment.</p><h3>Signature — Bind Essence</h3><p>Add traits and supernatural creature/material properties the base item does not normally possess.</p><h3>Mastery — Deep Binding</h3><p>Higher-tier work supports stronger creature-derived properties and more complex essence interactions.</p><h3>Legacy — Essence Workshops</h3><p>Converts monster, planar and environmental essences into reusable crafting components.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-2-minor-binding\"><h4>Minor Binding</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>At creation add two descriptive utility tags from the component&#39;s source, such as luminous or water-resistant. They unlock compatible crafting requirements but grant no numerical Core progression or creature immunities.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Essencebinding · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-2-bound-trait\"><h4>Bound Trait</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Weapon gains two chosen compatible traits from trip, shove, disarm or versatile B/P/S. Record the exact traits at creation. This does not add reach, deadly or fatal.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Essencebinding · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 1 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-2-elemental-essence\"><h4>Elemental Essence</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Weapon deals additional Core Tier d8 damage of a selected acid, cold, electricity or fire type. Worn armor or held shield instead grants resistance equal to 5 × Core Tier to that type. Resistance uses the highest source.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Essencebinding · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 1 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-2-predatory-essence\"><h4>Predatory Essence</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Choose at creation either precise darkvision 60 feet, imprecise scent 30 feet, climb Speed 30 feet or swim Speed 30 feet from the harvested essence. Active while worn or wielded; the choice is fixed until recrafted.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Essencebinding · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 1 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-2-greater-binding\"><h4>Greater Binding</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Weapon gains +5 feet reach and +2 additional base weapon damage dice. These extra dice use the weapon&#39;s die size and damage type; reach does not improve ranged attacks. Over-Striking stacks with different Marks.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Essencebinding · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 2 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-2-living-essence\"><h4>Living Essence</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 2 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Two actions, once per day for 1 minute: gain fly Speed equal to land Speed and resistance equal to 4 × Core Tier to the essence&#39;s one chosen energy type. Choose one type at creation from acid, cold, electricity or fire; no immunity is granted.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Essencebinding · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 2 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article></div><h2>Runecarving</h2><p>Efficient rune creation, upgrading, transfer, and linked Rune Echoes.</p><h3>Signature — Runic Logic</h3><p>Build persistent sigils and linked magical logic into equipment; this replaces the old assumption that normal PF2e property runes still exist.</p><h3>Mastery — Rune Resonance</h3><p>Linked sigils are easier to upgrade and can interact across paired items.</p><h3>Legacy — Runic Infrastructure</h3><p>Supports ward arrays, military sigils and public magical systems.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-3-runic-signature\"><h4>Runic Signature</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>While worn or held, gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Arcana checks involving this artisan&#39;s sigils. Enable the Mark condition only for those sigils.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Runecarving · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-3-resonant-pair\"><h4>Resonant Pair</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Link two paid items at creation. While both are worn or wielded within 30 feet, each bearer gains +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to saves against the last creature damaged by the other bearer this round. Track the eligible creature manually.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Runecarving · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 1 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-3-layered-inscription\"><h4>Layered Inscription</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Choose one Standard Mark on this item and record three legal configurations of its existing choices. Switch one configuration during daily preparations; this does not grant all three benefits or bypass prerequisites.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Runecarving · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 1 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-3-runic-feedback\"><h4>Runic Feedback</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Reaction</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Reaction, once per round when a linked weapon within 30 feet critically hits: its paired bearer gains +5 Artisan Bonus to their next attack or save before the end of their next turn. A bearer cannot trigger this from their own attack.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Runecarving · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 1 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-3-living-rune\"><h4>Living Rune</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 1 Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>One action, once per round: switch one Major-or-lower Mark between two recorded, equally costed configurations. Used charges and frequency limits remain spent across configurations; switching cannot refresh effects.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Runecarving · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 2 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-3-grand-glyph\"><h4>Grand Glyph</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 3 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Three actions, once per day: place a visible 20-foot-radius glyph within 60 feet for 1 minute. Allies in it gain +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to AC. Enemies starting turns inside take Core Tier d8 force damage, basic Reflex save against your higher class or spell DC. The glyph is stationary.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Runecarving · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 2 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article></div></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00014","name":"Leatherwork — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1400000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Leatherwork — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>High-power campaign revision: all 253 Marks have been reviewed. Flat Artisan bonuses stack; resistances use the highest applicable source. Capacity and the one-free-Mark limit still apply.</p><p>Campaign descriptions are not a promise that every effect is automated. Supported passive numbers use the item rules; activations, auras, project changes and special riders require manual resolution unless stated otherwise. Native action readouts do not spend uses automatically. Structure Marks never grant character bonuses.</p><p>Where a Mark grants a separate 10-point temporary-HP buffer, track it alongside class temporary HP. Spend the Artisan buffer first, then ordinary temporary HP, then HP. Different Mark buffers may coexist; the same grant cannot refill through re-equipping and expires as written. Maximum-HP increases are not healing.</p><h2>Universal Artisan Marks</h2><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-universal-flexible-construction\"><h4>Flexible Construction</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Reduce this armor&#39;s land Speed penalty by 10 feet, minimum 0. It does not grant bonus Speed if the penalty is already absent.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-universal-perfect-fit\"><h4>Supple Gussets</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to Acrobatics checks to Squeeze. Physical passage size restrictions still apply.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-universal-reinforced-hide\"><h4>Tanner&#39;s Acid Ward</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants acid resistance equal to 3 × Core Tier. Resistance uses the highest applicable source, not their sum.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 1 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-universal-weather-seal\"><h4>Weather Seal</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Fortitude saves against environmental heat, cold or exposure. Enable the Mark condition only for exposure, not energy attacks.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 1 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-universal-adaptive-strapping\"><h4>Adaptive Strapping</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Once per round, draw or stow one strapped light item as part of an Interact action using that item. Also secure up to three such items against accidental loss; deliberate Disarm and theft are unaffected.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 1 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article></div><h2>Wyrmcraft</h2><p>Dragon-scale equipment that preserves an adaptation belonging to the source dragon.</p><h3>Signature — Draconic Essence</h3><p>Preserve and exploit qualities from dragon type, colour and age in armour, weapons and reinforcement. Dragon Scale Core and Reinforcement already provide native colour resistance; Wyrmcraft deepens or transforms that inheritance.</p><h3>Mastery — Perfect Harvest</h3><p>Gain more usable dragon material and reduce waste while preparing scales and hides.</p><h3>Legacy — Dragonworks</h3><p>Creates elite army equipment, prestige goods, diplomatic trophies and draconic settlement works.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-1-wyrm-inscription\"><h4>Wyrm Inscription</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>The dragon&#39;s identity is visible on the item. While wielded or worn, gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Arcana checks about that dragon type. Enable the Mark condition only for that subject.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-1-draconic-resistance\"><h4>Draconic Resistance</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Requires Dragon Scale Core or Reinforcement. Add 3 × Dragon Tier to this item&#39;s native dragon resistance. This increases one resistance source, not all of the wearer&#39;s resistances.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 1 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-1-scale-dominion\"><h4>Scale Dominion</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Requires Dragon Scale Core or Reinforcement. Armor or shield gains +5 × Dragon Tier Hardness and +30 × Dragon Tier item HP. A weapon instead ignores 3 × Dragon Tier resistance against its associated dragon damage type; immunity remains.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 1 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-1-draconic-constitution\"><h4>Draconic Constitution</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Requires Dragon Scale Core or Reinforcement. Worn armor grants +16 × Dragon Tier maximum HP and +5 Artisan Bonus to saves against its associated damage type; green scales apply to poison. Maximum HP is not healing.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 1 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-1-wyrms-fury\"><h4>Wyrm&#39;s Fury</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Requires Dragon Scale Core or Reinforcement. Weapon gains +3 additional base weapon damage dice, using its existing die size and damage type. This Over-Striking stacks with different Marks.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 2 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-1-dragonheart-awakening\"><h4>Dragonheart Awakening</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 2 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Two actions, once per day for 1 minute: gain fly Speed equal to twice land Speed and increase this item&#39;s native dragon resistance by 5 × Dragon Tier. Once during the duration, use two actions for a 30-foot cone dealing 3 × Dragon Tier d8 of the scale&#39;s damage type, basic Reflex against your higher class or spell DC.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 2 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article></div><h2>Beastbinding</h2><p>Prepared hides that preserve a useful natural quality of the creature they came from.</p><h3>Signature — Preserve the Beast</h3><p>Retain a natural or supernatural quality from the creature whose hide/material was used.</p><h3>Mastery — Master Harvester</h3><p>Improve creature-material yield and preserve delicate traits that ordinary harvesting would destroy.</p><h3>Legacy — Monstercraft Trade</h3><p>Turns rare creature materials into specialist exports and campaign resources.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-2-trophy-memory\"><h4>Trophy Memory</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>While worn or wielded, gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Nature checks to Recall Knowledge about the source creature family. Enable the Mark condition only for that family.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Beastbinding · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-2-predators-sense\"><h4>Predator&#39;s Sense</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>While worn, gain imprecise scent 30 feet and +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Survival checks to Track the source creature family. Scent detects presence, not precise location; record the source family on the item.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Beastbinding · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 1 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-2-natural-movement\"><h4>Natural Movement</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Choose a source-appropriate climb or swim Speed at creation. Worn armor grants that Speed at 40 feet and +10 feet to land Speed in one recorded natural terrain. Terrain does not change during combat.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Beastbinding · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 1 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-2-apex-hide\"><h4>Apex Hide</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants +10 × Core Tier maximum HP and +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Fortitude saves against one recorded creature theme: poison, cold or disease. This replaces the former start-of-combat temporary HP grant.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Beastbinding · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 1 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-2-apex-trait\"><h4>Apex Trait</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants imprecise tremorsense 30 feet while you share a solid surface with the target, and doubles your ordinary Leap distance. Tremorsense does not detect airborne creatures or bypass concealment.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Beastbinding · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 2 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-2-chimera-binding\"><h4>Chimera Binding</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Free Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Free action once per round: select one of two recorded creature-source senses or movement modes for this item. Once per day, both can be active for 10 minutes. Pay for both source components; no access to unrecorded creature abilities.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Beastbinding · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 2 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article></div><h2>Mantlecraft</h2><p>Prestigious and protective mantles, cloaks, robes, and environmental garments.</p><h3>Signature — Great Mantles</h3><p>Create exceptional cloaks, coats, ceremonial furs and environmental garments.</p><h3>Mastery — Luxury Craftsmanship</h3><p>Reduce rare-fur waste and substantially increase trade/prestige value.</p><h3>Legacy — Royal Clothier</h3><p>Supports diplomacy, gifts, court prestige and luxury industry.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-3-trophy-finish\"><h4>Trophy Finish</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Intimidation checks when the visible trophy is relevant to the audience. Enable the Mark condition only then; it is not mental control.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Mantlecraft · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-3-weather-mantle\"><h4>Whiteout Mantle</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants cold resistance equal to 5 × Core Tier and an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier to Survival. It does not grant weather immunity.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Mantlecraft · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 1 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-3-predators-cloak\"><h4>Predator&#39;s Cloak</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Free Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Stealth and Survival in one recorded terrain. Free action once per round after successfully Hiding there: Step up to 10 feet. The terrain must match the trophy&#39;s source.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Mantlecraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 1 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-3-court-mantle\"><h4>Court Mantle</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Diplomacy and Society in formal settings. Allies within 15 feet who can see you gain +3 Artisan Bonus to saves against fear while you are conscious; adjudicate the aura manually.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Mantlecraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 1 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-3-sovereign-pelt\"><h4>Dread Sovereign Pelt</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to Intimidation and Survival. A predator&#39;s presence dominates the hunt and the negotiation table without removing social consequences.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Mantlecraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 2 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-3-legendary-pelt\"><h4>Legendary Pelt</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 1 Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>One action, once per day for 1 minute: become invisible. After each hostile action the invisibility is suppressed until the start of your next turn. While invisible this way, gain +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Stealth; invisibility is not undetectability.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Mantlecraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 2 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article></div></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00015","name":"Carpentry — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1500000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Carpentry — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>High-power campaign revision: all 253 Marks have been reviewed. Flat Artisan bonuses stack; resistances use the highest applicable source. Capacity and the one-free-Mark limit still apply.</p><p>Campaign descriptions are not a promise that every effect is automated. Supported passive numbers use the item rules; activations, auras, project changes and special riders require manual resolution unless stated otherwise. Native action readouts do not spend uses automatically. Structure Marks never grant character bonuses.</p><p>Where a Mark grants a separate 10-point temporary-HP buffer, track it alongside class temporary HP. Spend the Artisan buffer first, then ordinary temporary HP, then HP. Different Mark buffers may coexist; the same grant cannot refill through re-equipping and expires as written. Maximum-HP increases are not healing.</p><h2>Universal Artisan Marks</h2><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-universal-seasoned-construction\"><h4>Seasoned Construction</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Wooden armor or shield resists mundane warping and gains +100% of pre-Mark maximum item HP. This additive durability bonus does not multiply other Mark bonuses.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-universal-light-frame\"><h4>Light Frame</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Reduce Bulk by 2, minimum 0, when the wooden frame forms most of this item. Contents and attached equipment retain their own Bulk.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-universal-precision-joinery\"><h4>Precision Joinery</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>While held or worn, gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Crafting checks to Repair this item or operate its mechanism. Enable the Mark condition only for that mechanism.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 1 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-universal-reinforced-limb\"><h4>Skyhunter Limbs</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>A ranged weapon deals +3 × Core Tier damage against flying or falling targets. Enable the Mark condition only against an airborne target.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 1 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-universal-modular-frame\"><h4>Modular Frame</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Project</p><p>During daily preparations replace up to three ordinary wooden components with paid compatible alternatives. Retain legal Marks and maker records; no free resources, Capacity or extra active Core progression.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 1 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article></div><h2>Warbowyer</h2><p>Engineered bows, crossbows, ballistae, loading systems, and specialist ammunition.</p><h3>Signature — Engineered Ranged Weapons</h3><p>Build bows, crossbows, ballistae, specialist ammunition and advanced loading mechanisms.</p><h3>Mastery — Master Fletching</h3><p>Produce ammunition efficiently and maintain engineered ranged weapons with reduced waste.</p><h3>Legacy — Missile Industry</h3><p>Improves army archers, towers, ballistae and settlement ranged defence.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-1-true-fletching\"><h4>True Fletching</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Ranged weapon gains +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to attacks affected by ordinary wind. Enable the Mark condition only during such wind. Magical wind and range penalties remain.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Warbowyer · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-1-specialist-ammo-chamber\"><h4>Specialist Ammo Chamber</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Ranged weapon accepts two recorded compatible specialist ammunition families. Ammunition is paid and consumed normally; this does not enable ammunition of the wrong weapon category.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Warbowyer · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 1 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-1-longshot-construction\"><h4>Longshot Construction</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Double this ranged weapon&#39;s range increment. Normal increment penalties and line of effect still apply; this does not increase melee reach.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Warbowyer · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 1 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-1-rapid-mechanism\"><h4>Rapid Mechanism</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Free Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Free action once per round: reload this ranged weapon by up to two Interact actions. Supply ammunition and a free hand normally. A reload-0 weapon instead gains +5 Artisan Bonus to its next Strike this turn; these options are exclusive.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Warbowyer · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 1 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-1-perfected-tension\"><h4>Horizonstring</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>A ranged weapon grants +2 Artisan Bonus to attacks against targets beyond its first range increment. This Over-Potency bonus is capped at +2 per Mark. Enable the Mark condition only at that distance. Normal range penalties still apply.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Warbowyer · Core Tier 4+; Core-tier Anchor required</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 2 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-1-warbow-overdraw\"><h4>Warbow Overdraw</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Ranged weapon gains +3 additional base weapon damage dice using its own die size and type. After a natural 1 on a Strike, you are off-guard until the start of your next turn. Over-Striking stacks with different Marks.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Warbowyer · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 2 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article></div><h2>Masterwright</h2><p>Bridges, roads, docks, fieldworks, buildings, and major wooden structures.</p><h3>Signature — Great Works</h3><p>Build bridges, roads, palisades, docks, towers, camps and major wooden infrastructure.</p><h3>Mastery — Efficient Construction</h3><p>Reduce Lumber cost and repair downtime for qualifying projects.</p><h3>Legacy — Kingdom Builder</h3><p>Improves construction throughput, roads, fortifications, settlement expansion and repairs.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-2-builders-mark\"><h4>Builder&#39;s Mark</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Structure</p><p>Inspecting this wooden construction grants +Core Tier + 2 to Crafting checks to identify weaknesses or plan repairs. The mark records load paths; no actor effect is created.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Masterwright · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-2-reinforced-frame\"><h4>Reinforced Frame</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Structure</p><p>Wooden structure or vehicle gains ×3 pre-Mark maximum HP and +4 × Core Tier Hardness. Other durability bonuses add from the same base rather than compounding.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Masterwright · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 1 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-2-rapid-assembly\"><h4>Rapid Assembly</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Structure</p><p>Qualifying construction or field fortification takes half its original artisan-days, minimum one. Apply once to original work, not recursively after other reductions.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Masterwright · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 1 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-2-modular-construction\"><h4>Modular Construction</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Structure</p><p>Recover 90% of recorded ordinary inputs when dismantling, rounded down; unique inputs require GM adjudication. Re-deploy the stored modules in one-quarter normal assembly time, minimum 10 minutes.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Masterwright · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 1 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-2-grand-design\"><h4>Grand Design</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Structure</p><p>Choose recurring Lumber or repair cost: reduce it by 40%, minimum one unit. Gain +5 on the structure&#39;s principal construction check. These are campaign project benefits, not character Crafting bonuses.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Masterwright · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 2 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-2-citadel-framework\"><h4>Citadel Framework</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Structure</p><p>Defenders gain +5 to checks and saves against forced entry, collapse and siege movement while within the fortification. Gates and walls gain structural damage resistance equal to 8 × Core Tier.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Masterwright · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 2 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article></div><h2>Warcarving</h2><p>Combat forms and utility carvings applied to wooden weapons, shields, and tools.</p><h3>Signature — Carved Form</h3><p>Add combat identities and totemic properties to wooden weapons, shields and tools.</p><h3>Mastery — Deep Carving</h3><p>Preserve increasingly complex magical/totemic carvings without weakening the wood.</p><h3>Legacy — Carved Traditions</h3><p>Supports ceremonial weapons, military equipment and cultural relics.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-3-carved-grip\"><h4>Carved Grip</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Gain +Core Tier + 2 to your DC against Disarm attempts targeting this weapon. It does not protect other held items or prevent voluntary dropping.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Warcarving · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-3-wolf-carving\"><h4>Wolf Carving</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Free Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Free action once per round after this weapon hits: Stride up to half Speed toward that target. Movement must end closer and triggers reactions normally.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Warcarving · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 1 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-3-bear-carving\"><h4>Bear Carving</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>While this shield is raised, gain +2 Artisan Bonus to AC for a tower or fortress shield, +1 for other non-buckler shields, or no extra AC for a buckler. This adds to normal raised-shield AC and does not grant cover. While raised, gain physical resistance equal to 3 × Core Tier; against damage caused by forced movement, use 6 × Core Tier instead. Use only the applicable resistance value, not both.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Warcarving · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 1 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-3-serpent-carving\"><h4>Serpent Carving</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Free Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Weapon gains +5 feet melee reach. Free action once per round after hitting: Step up to 15 feet; this movement does not trigger that target&#39;s reactions. Other creatures react normally if applicable.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Warcarving · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 1 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-3-spirit-carving\"><h4>Spirit Carving</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 1 Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>One action, once per encounter for 1 minute: gain +5 Artisan Bonus to this weapon&#39;s attacks and imprecise scent 30 feet. This is a magical spirit manifestation; it grants no extra actions.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Warcarving · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 2 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-3-totemic-ascendance\"><h4>Totemic Ascendance</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 2 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Two actions, once per day for 1 minute: gain +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Athletics, +20 feet land Speed and resistance equal to 4 × Core Tier to physical damage. A visible animal spirit surrounds the wearer.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Warcarving · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 2 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article></div></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00016","name":"Stonemasonry — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1600000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Stonemasonry — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>High-power campaign revision: all 253 Marks have been reviewed. Flat Artisan bonuses stack; resistances use the highest applicable source. Capacity and the one-free-Mark limit still apply.</p><p>Campaign descriptions are not a promise that every effect is automated. Supported passive numbers use the item rules; activations, auras, project changes and special riders require manual resolution unless stated otherwise. Native action readouts do not spend uses automatically. Structure Marks never grant character bonuses.</p><p>Where a Mark grants a separate 10-point temporary-HP buffer, track it alongside class temporary HP. Spend the Artisan buffer first, then ordinary temporary HP, then HP. Different Mark buffers may coexist; the same grant cannot refill through re-equipping and expires as written. Maximum-HP increases are not healing.</p><h2>Universal Artisan Marks</h2><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-universal-stonebound\"><h4>Stonebound</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Armor or shield gains +50% of its pre-Mark maximum item HP and +2 × Core Tier Hardness. The stone protects the item, not its wearer&#39;s HP. Durability bonuses add against the same pre-Mark base.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-universal-perfect-foundation\"><h4>Perfect Foundation</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Structure</p><p>Gain +Core Tier + 2 on checks to stabilise or repair a structure built on this foundation. Its reference lines reveal subsidence before ordinary collapse.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-universal-anchored-construction\"><h4>Anchored Construction</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Structure</p><p>Structure gains +Core Tier + 2 to its DC against forced movement or toppling and counts as two sizes larger for those contests. It can still be damaged or destroyed.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 1 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-universal-load-bearing-cut\"><h4>Load-Bearing Cut</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Structure</p><p>Stone structure gains +100% of pre-Mark maximum HP. This adds to other durability bonuses using the same base; it does not grant character HP.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 1 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-universal-resonant-stone\"><h4>Resonant Stone</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Project</p><p>The component can provide both ward and arcane-anchor tags for compatible work. Tags grant eligibility only, not extra Capacity, Core progression or free Marks.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 1 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article></div><h2>Megalithics</h2><p>Monumental works, fortresses, roads, aqueducts, walls, and major civil structures.</p><h3>Signature — Great Works</h3><p>Create fortresses, roads, aqueducts, monumental walls, towers and vast stone projects.</p><h3>Mastery — Monumental Engineering</h3><p>Reduce Stone waste and repair time for major works.</p><h3>Legacy — Civilisation Builder</h3><p>Transforms settlements through enduring infrastructure and wonders.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-1-masons-seal\"><h4>Mason&#39;s Seal</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Structure</p><p>Gain +Core Tier + 2 on Crafting checks to identify damage, load paths or reconstruction methods in the sealed stonework. Inspection reveals non-magical hidden cavities within 5 feet of the examined surface.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Megalithics · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-1-enduring-monument\"><h4>Enduring Monument</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Structure</p><p>Monument has ×4 pre-Mark maximum HP and +5 × Core Tier Hardness. Durability bonuses add from the pre-Mark base rather than multiplying one another.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Megalithics · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 1 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-1-grand-foundation\"><h4>Grand Foundation</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Structure</p><p>Structures on this foundation gain +5 against collapse, subsidence and siege movement. Repairs restore twice normal item HP without consuming additional ordinary repair materials.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Megalithics · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 1 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-1-civic-wonder\"><h4>Civic Wonder</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Structure</p><p>Choose Culture, Defence, Trade, Faith or Infrastructure at creation. Once per Kingdom turn gain +5 on one project check directly serving that purpose. The wonder also acts as a recognised landmark; no automatic income is created.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Megalithics · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 1 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-1-imperial-work\"><h4>Imperial Work</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Structure</p><p>Reduce one named recurring Kingdom resource cost tied to this structure by 40%, minimum one unit. Once per Kingdom turn reroll one failed maintenance check for it and use the new result.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Megalithics · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 2 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-1-world-rooted-foundation\"><h4>World-Rooted Foundation</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Structure</p><p>The structure cannot be moved or toppled by non-magical effects. It gains structural damage resistance equal to 12 × Core Tier; magical displacement requires a counteract check against the completed project&#39;s recorded DC.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Megalithics · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 2 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article></div><h2>Runemasonry</h2><p>Wardstones and enduring magical inscriptions that protect places rather than carried items.</p><h3>Signature — Wardstones</h3><p>Bind magical zones, alarms, protections and restrictions to locations rather than carried items.</p><h3>Mastery — Deep Inscription</h3><p>Increase ward area, duration and magical stability.</p><h3>Legacy — Great Wards</h3><p>Protects settlements from intrusion, teleportation, undead, weather and magical assault.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-2-inscribed-keystone\"><h4>Inscribed Keystone</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Structure</p><p>Gain +Core Tier + 2 on checks to identify or repair this ward. Authorised users can read its owner, purpose and whether it has been breached.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Runemasonry · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-2-sentinel-rune\"><h4>Sentinel Rune</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Structure</p><p>Detect a recorded creature trait crossing the site&#39;s boundary within 300 feet of the rune. Alert up to six designated creatures anywhere inside the site; this is an alarm, not precise tracking or a hostile effect.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Runemasonry · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 1 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-2-sanctuary-ward\"><h4>Sanctuary Ward</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Structure</p><p>A stationary 30-foot zone grants authorised allies +5 to saves while inside. Once per creature per day on entering, restore 10 × Core Tier HP. Leaving and re-entering does not refresh healing.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Runemasonry · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 1 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-2-war-rune\"><h4>War Rune</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Structure</p><p>In a stationary 30-foot zone, authorised defenders gain +5 to attack rolls and +3 × Core Tier damage on their first successful Strike each round. The rune does not move with a bearer.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Runemasonry · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 1 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-2-fortress-sigil\"><h4>Fortress Sigil</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Structure</p><p>Hostile teleportation or planar entry into the recorded site requires a counteract check against the project&#39;s recorded DC +5. Failure prevents entry and spends the attempt normally; authorised travel is unaffected.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Runemasonry · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 2 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-2-dominion-ward\"><h4>Dominion Ward</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Structure</p><p>One recorded hostile creature trait suffers -5 to attacks and saves within a 60-foot ward. Those creatures cannot use ordinary concealment against authorised defenders; invisibility and total cover remain unless separately overcome.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Runemasonry · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 2 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article></div><h2>Titanmasonry</h2><p>Stone wargear, constructs, siege engines, and powerful Titanic forms.</p><h3>Signature — Titanic Construction</h3><p>Create stone armour, colossal shields, siege devices, constructs and crushing wargear.</p><h3>Mastery — Mountaincraft</h3><p>Make enormous stone components usable without losing impossible stability.</p><h3>Legacy — Stone Legions</h3><p>Supports constructs, fortifications and siege warfare.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-3-titanic-fit\"><h4>Titanic Fit</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Ignore up to 3 Bulk belonging to this stone item while properly worn or wielded, minimum 0. Contents and other equipment are unaffected.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-3-anchored\"><h4>Anchored</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>While worn or raised, gain +5 to the DC against Trip or Reposition and count as two sizes larger for resisting forced movement. This does not increase your actual size or offensive manoeuvre limits.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 1 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-3-earthshaker\"><h4>Earthshaker</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Free Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Free action once per round after a critical weapon hit or successful Shield Block: choose an adjacent enemy. Fortitude against your higher class/spell DC: failure pushes it 10 feet and makes it off-guard until the end of its next turn; critical failure also knocks it prone. No effect on success.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 1 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-3-mountain-plate\"><h4>Basalt Bastion</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants physical resistance equal to 3 × Core Tier and an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier to Fortitude saves.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 1 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-3-mountain-blood-plate\"><h4>Heart of the Mountain</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants physical resistance equal to 5 × Core Tier, an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to Fortitude saves, and -5 feet to land Speed. Physical resistances use the highest source.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 2 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-3-living-colossus\"><h4>Living Colossus</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 2 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Two actions, once per day for 1 minute: grow one size category, gain +10 feet melee reach, +5 Artisan Bonus to Athletics and physical resistance equal to 5 × Core Tier. End in sufficient space; equipment enlarges but its sale value and permanent Bulk do not change.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 2 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article></div></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00017","name":"Glassmaking — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1700000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Glassmaking — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>High-power campaign revision: all 253 Marks have been reviewed. Flat Artisan bonuses stack; resistances use the highest applicable source. Capacity and the one-free-Mark limit still apply.</p><p>Campaign descriptions are not a promise that every effect is automated. Supported passive numbers use the item rules; activations, auras, project changes and special riders require manual resolution unless stated otherwise. Native action readouts do not spend uses automatically. Structure Marks never grant character bonuses.</p><p>Where a Mark grants a separate 10-point temporary-HP buffer, track it alongside class temporary HP. Spend the Artisan buffer first, then ordinary temporary HP, then HP. Different Mark buffers may coexist; the same grant cannot refill through re-equipping and expires as written. Maximum-HP increases are not healing.</p><h2>Universal Artisan Marks</h2><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-universal-perfect-clarity\"><h4>Perfect Clarity</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · 3 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>A held optic grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Perception checks involving visual detail. Enable the Mark condition only when viewing through the optic; it does not bypass concealment. Stored Flare — Three actions (Concentrate, Manipulate, Light), once per day: release stored light in a 15-foot emanation. Creatures other than you attempt a Fortitude save against your higher class or spell DC: failure dazzled for Core Tier rounds; critical failure blinded for 1 round, then dazzled for Core Tier rounds; success unaffected. Resolve saves and conditions manually. This is a visual effect.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-universal-hardened-glass\"><h4>Glarecut Glass</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>A held focus grants an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to visual Seek checks. Enable the Mark condition when sight applies; concealment is not negated.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-universal-arcane-lens\"><h4>Arcane Lens</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Project</p><p>The optical component grants arcane, optic and conductor tags and can provide two compatible lens sockets. Supply their materials and Marks normally; no Capacity increase.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 1 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-universal-precision-focus\"><h4>Precision Focus</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · 2 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Ranged weapon gains +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to attacks against a target you successfully Sought this turn using the mounted optic. Enable the Mark condition only for that target and turn. Prismatic Sightline — Two actions, once per encounter: Seek using the optic, then make one ranged Strike with this weapon against a creature you detected. Ignore ordinary concealment for that Strike, but not hidden, undetected or total cover. Normal multiple attack penalty applies.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 1 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-universal-shatter-safe\"><h4>Shatter Safe</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Reaction</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Twice per day when damage would destroy this glass-bearing item, it instead remains at 1 item HP. This protects the item only; worn-item protection does not prevent bearer damage. Record spent uses manually. Shatter Ward — Reaction. Trigger: damage would destroy this item. Spend one of this Mark&#39;s two daily uses to leave it at 1 item HP instead. This is the activation cost of its existing protection, not additional uses; it never prevents damage to the bearer.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 1 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Prismcraft</h2><p>Lenses and prisms that focus, split, redirect, or transform light and magical energy.</p><h3>Signature — Arcane Optics</h3><p>Focus, split, redirect and transform light or magical energy with precision lenses and prisms.</p><h3>Mastery — Perfect Refraction</h3><p>Safely handle stronger magical energy and reduce material loss in advanced optical components.</p><h3>Legacy — Observatory Craft</h3><p>Supports surveying, astronomy, navigation, signalling and watchtowers.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-1-calibrated-lens\"><h4>Surveyor&#39;s Reticle</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>A held focus grants an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier to initiative. Read the battlefield before the first blow.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Prismcraft · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-1-focusing-lens\"><h4>Focusing Lens</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Increase the ranged weapon&#39;s range increment by 50%. The mounted optical sight does not affect melee reach or remove range penalties.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Prismcraft · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 1 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-1-spectrum-prism\"><h4>Spectrum Prism</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Free Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Choose two energy types from acid, cold, electricity or fire at creation. Free action once per round before this weapon&#39;s Strike: convert all its added energy damage from the first type to the second, or back. Base physical damage is unchanged.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Prismcraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 1 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-1-beam-splitter\"><h4>Beam Splitter</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Reaction</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Reaction, once per encounter after a ranged weapon Strike hits: make a second Strike against a different target within 30 feet of the first, using the same multiple attack penalty as the triggering Strike. This additional Strike counts toward later attacks; pay ammunition normally.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Prismcraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 1 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-1-trueglass-crown\"><h4>Trueglass Crown</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor reveals invisible creatures to you within 60 feet as concealed rather than invisible. Gain +5 Artisan Bonus to saves against visual illusions. It does not see through walls or automatically disbelieve illusions.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Prismcraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 2 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-1-crown-prism\"><h4>Sovereign Refraction</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>A held spell focus grants +2 Artisan Bonus to spell DC and +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Arcana, with a -1 Artisan spell-attack penalty. The Over-Potency spell DC bonus is capped at +2 per Mark. Requires a Tier 5+ optical Anchor. Its power favours save spells.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Prismcraft · Core Tier 4+; Core-tier Anchor required</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 2 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Mirrorcraft</h2><p>Reflective magic, illusions, scrying, communication, and linked mirrors.</p><h3>Signature — Reflection</h3><p>Create supernatural mirrors for illusion, scrying, communication, defence and travel.</p><h3>Mastery — Perfect Reflection</h3><p>Safely reflect or retain increasingly powerful magical phenomena.</p><h3>Legacy — Mirror Network</h3><p>Links settlements for communication, intelligence and eventually transport.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-2-perfect-reflection\"><h4>Perfect Reflection</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>A held focus grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Deception checks to Impersonate using the mirror to prepare your disguise. Enable the Mark condition only for that prepared disguise.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-2-truth-mirror\"><h4>Truth Mirror</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · 1 Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>A held focus grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Perception checks to Sense Motive or detect a visual disguise through the mirror. Enable the Mark condition only for those checks; no automatic lie detection. Unmask — One action, once per encounter: attempt to counteract one visual illusion affecting a creature or object seen through the mirror within 30 feet. Use your higher class or spell DC minus 10 for the counteract modifier and Core Tier as counteract rank. Ordinary disguises instead permit one immediate Seek check.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 1 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-2-reflective-ward\"><h4>Reflective Ward</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Reaction</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Reaction, once per encounter when a spell attack targets you: gain +5 Artisan Bonus to AC against that attack. If it critically misses, deal Core Tier d8 force damage to its caster within 60 feet, basic Reflex against your higher class/spell DC. This is retaliation, not a copied spell.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 1 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-2-doppelglass\"><h4>Doppelglass</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · 1 Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>One action, once per encounter: gain concealed until the start of your next turn. The first attack that misses because of this flat check lets you Step 10 feet as a free action; this movement does not end the concealment.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 1 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-2-gate-mirror\"><h4>Gate Mirror</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 3 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Three actions, once per day: open a two-way portal between this mirror and its paid, attuned partner within 10 miles on the same plane for 1 minute. Up to six willing creatures may cross. Both exits require open space; dimensional wards can block passage.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 2 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-2-mirror-lord\"><h4>Mirror Lord</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 2 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Two actions, once per day for 1 minute: once per round use your reaction when targeted by a spell attack to counteract it using your higher class/spell DC minus 10 and counteract rank equal to Core Tier. Success negates it; critical success also deals 2 × Core Tier d8 force damage to the caster, basic Reflex against that DC.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 2 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Aetherglass</h2><p>Mana batteries, spell reservoirs, magical circuitry, construct cores, and powered components.</p><h3>Signature — Mana Conduction</h3><p>Build mana batteries, spell reservoirs, magical circuitry and construct cores.</p><h3>Mastery — Aether Cells</h3><p>Store progressively greater magical energy with less loss and safer discharge.</p><h3>Legacy — Arcane Grid</h3><p>Powers large-scale magical infrastructure and magitek networks.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-3-stable-cell\"><h4>Stable Cell</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Recorded magical charges cannot decay from ordinary time or environmental exposure. Once per day ignore one effect that would drain a single charge; this does not stop deliberate use or regenerate spent charges.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Aetherglass · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-3-mana-reservoir\"><h4>Mana Reservoir</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · 2 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Add three daily charges to one named custom activation on this item. Charges cannot fuel recovery, extra-charge or refresh effects and return only at daily preparations. Reservoir Lance — Two actions, once per encounter: expend one charge from the named pool to deal 2 × Core Tier d6 force damage to one creature within 60 feet, basic Reflex against your higher class or spell DC. This does not restore or create charges; resolve damage and charge spending manually.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Aetherglass · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 1 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-3-arcane-conductor\"><h4>Arcane Conductor</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Weapon gains +2 additional base weapon damage dice from a luminous glass channel. Use its existing die size and type; this Over-Striking stacks with different Marks.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Aetherglass · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 1 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-3-overflow-channel\"><h4>Overflow Channel</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Free Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Free action once per encounter before a damaging item activation: add Core Tier d8 damage of that activation&#39;s primary damage type. If it costs charges, pay one additional charge. Applies once to one damage roll, not persistent or repeated damage.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Aetherglass · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 1 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-3-crystal-matrix\"><h4>Crystal Matrix</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Project</p><p>Reduce the Capacity cost of one compatible paid Enchanting or Azlanti Artifice Mark by 2, minimum 1. Does not grant a free Mark or raise maximum Capacity. Multiple discounts apply to the original cost, never below 1.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Aetherglass · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 2 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-3-eternity-cell\"><h4>Eternity Cell</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Add five charges per day to one named custom activation. Once per encounter when you critically succeed at an attack or save, recover one charge spent on that activation. Cannot fuel charge generation, resource recovery, healing or refresh effects.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Aetherglass · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 2 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00018","name":"Pottery — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1800000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Pottery — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>High-power campaign revision: all 253 Marks have been reviewed. Flat Artisan bonuses stack; resistances use the highest applicable source. Capacity and the one-free-Mark limit still apply.</p><p>Campaign descriptions are not a promise that every effect is automated. Supported passive numbers use the item rules; activations, auras, project changes and special riders require manual resolution unless stated otherwise. Native action readouts do not spend uses automatically. Structure Marks never grant character bonuses.</p><p>Where a Mark grants a separate 10-point temporary-HP buffer, track it alongside class temporary HP. Spend the Artisan buffer first, then ordinary temporary HP, then HP. Different Mark buffers may coexist; the same grant cannot refill through re-equipping and expires as written. Maximum-HP increases are not healing.</p><h2>Universal Artisan Marks</h2><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-universal-hardened-ceramic\"><h4>Emberproof Glaze</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor or a held shield grants fire resistance equal to 3 × Core Tier. Resistance uses the highest applicable source.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-universal-thermal-craft\"><h4>Thermal Craft</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Contents remain at their stored mundane temperature for 24 hours while sealed. The vessel ignores ordinary heat/cold damage from storage; attacks, spells and bearer damage are unaffected.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-universal-sealed-vessel\"><h4>Sealed Vessel</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Contents cannot leak, evaporate or become mundanely contaminated until the vessel is destroyed, not merely Broken. Does not preserve a consumed dose or increase storage capacity.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 1 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-universal-shock-fired\"><h4>Shock-Fired</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>The ceramic item gains +Core Tier + 2 to its DC or checks against shattering and rupture effects. This is item protection, not a bonus to the bearer&#39;s saves.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 1 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-universal-nested-chamber\"><h4>Nested Chamber</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · 1 Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Add three concealed internal chambers, each holding one light dose or object. Their contents count toward Bulk; searching the chambers uses the normal concealment rules with +Core Tier + 2 to the item&#39;s concealment DC. Chamber Draw — One action (Manipulate): retrieve one object from a chamber into a free hand. This does not activate, drink or use the retrieved object; those actions retain their normal costs.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 1 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Ceramancy</h2><p>Living clay, terracotta constructs, ceramic armour, figurines, and guardians.</p><h3>Signature — Living Clay</h3><p>Create supernatural ceramics, terracotta guardians and adaptive ceramic armour.</p><h3>Mastery — Awakened Kiln</h3><p>Build increasingly complex animated ceramics with less breakage and better control.</p><h3>Legacy — Terracotta Works</h3><p>Supports workers, guardians, soldiers and settlement sentinels.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-1-fired-seal\"><h4>Fired Seal</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>While worn or held, gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Crafting checks to Repair or identify this ceramic item. Enable the Mark condition only when working on this item.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Ceramancy · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-1-ceramic-plate\"><h4>Ceramic Plate</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · 2 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Armor or shield gains +5 × Core Tier Hardness and +40 × Core Tier item HP without increased Bulk. This improves the item, not wearer maximum HP. Kiln Renewal — Two actions, once per encounter: touch the armor or shield to restore 8 × Core Tier item HP, up to its maximum. It must not be destroyed. This repairs the item, never its wearer&#39;s HP.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Ceramancy · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 1 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-1-living-clay\"><h4>Living Clay</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>At the start of the wearer&#39;s turn during an encounter, repair this item for 5 × Core Tier HP if it is not destroyed. Outside encounters it repairs once per minute. It cannot restore missing components or the wearer&#39;s HP.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Ceramancy · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 1 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-1-terracotta-guardian\"><h4>Terracotta Guardian</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · 3 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Three actions, once per day: animate a guardian for 1 minute using a creature stat block recorded at creation, maximum level equal to twice Core Tier. It has the minion trait and requires one action to command; no independent extra turns or summoning abilities. The GM approves the exact stat block.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Ceramancy · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 1 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-1-adaptive-ceramic\"><h4>Adaptive Ceramic</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Reaction</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Reaction once per round before taking bludgeoning, piercing or slashing damage: gain resistance equal to 6 × Core Tier against that type, including the triggering damage, until the start of your next turn. Other physical types are unaffected.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Ceramancy · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 2 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-1-living-ceramic-shell\"><h4>Living Ceramic Shell</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants +20 × Core Tier maximum HP. At the start of each encounter turn repair the armor itself for 4 × Core Tier item HP. Replaces regenerating temporary HP; removing or re-equipping grants no healing.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Ceramancy · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 2 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Reliquarycraft</h2><p>Vessels that preserve blessings, curses, spirits, essences, and planar energy.</p><h3>Signature — Vessel of Essence</h3><p>Capture and safely preserve supernatural essences, spirits, curses, blessings and planar energy.</p><h3>Mastery — Perfect Containment</h3><p>Safely house stronger and more volatile essences with less risk of leakage or corruption.</p><h3>Legacy — Great Reliquaries</h3><p>Supports temples, magical institutions, cursed-artifact storage and spirit containment.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-2-sanctified-vessel\"><h4>Sanctified Vessel</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>While holding the vessel, gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Religion checks to identify its contained essence. Enable the Mark condition for that essence only. Mundane spiritual leakage is prevented.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Reliquarycraft · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-2-essence-vessel\"><h4>Essence Vessel</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Project</p><p>Store up to three separately sealed harvested essences without ordinary degradation. They remain distinct paid inputs; opening one chamber does not consume or expose the others.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Reliquarycraft · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 1 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-2-bound-spirit\"><h4>Bound Spirit</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Record a willing spirit and one Lore at creation. While holding the vessel gain +5 Artisan Bonus to checks with that Lore; the spirit can speak to its bearer. It grants neither extra turns nor access to undisclosed creature abilities.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Reliquarycraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 1 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-2-sealed-curse\"><h4>Sealed Curse</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Project</p><p>A successfully contained curse cannot spread while this vessel remains intact. Gain +5 on attempts to counteract the contained curse using the normal counteract procedure. The containment itself requires resolving the curse, not simply placing this Mark.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Reliquarycraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 1 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-2-release-matrix\"><h4>Release Matrix</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 2 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Two actions, once per day: discharge one paid stored essence in a 30-foot cone for 3 × Core Tier d8 spirit damage, basic Will against your higher class/spell DC. Consume the essence; recharging requires another compatible harvested essence.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Reliquarycraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 2 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-2-grand-reliquary\"><h4>Grand Reliquary</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 2 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Hold three paid compatible essences. Two actions once per day: consume two to heal up to six willing creatures within 30 feet for 8 × Core Tier HP each and reduce their frightened by 2. Refilling does not reset the daily use.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Reliquarycraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 2 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Pyroceramics</h2><p>Crucibles, bomb casings, heat-resistant vessels, magical kilns, and industrial ceramics.</p><h3>Signature — Cruciblecraft</h3><p>Create bomb casings, furnaces, crucibles, pressure vessels and extreme-temperature components.</p><h3>Mastery — Grand Kiln</h3><p>Improve industrial/alchemical throughput and reduce failures when processing extreme heat materials.</p><h3>Legacy — Industrial Kilns</h3><p>Supports bricks, pipes, sanitation, forges, alchemy and mass production.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-3-heatproof-glaze\"><h4>Heatproof Glaze</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>The vessel ignores ordinary forge heat and gains +Core Tier + 2 to checks against magical thermal breakage. This does not protect the bearer from fire damage or create a resistance aura.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Pyroceramics · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-3-thermal-crucible\"><h4>Thermal Crucible</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Project</p><p>When processing heat-sensitive ordinary materials, recover 30% of otherwise lost units, rounded down. Recovery cannot exceed recorded loss and cannot be recycled through the same process for new material.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Pyroceramics · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 1 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-3-fragmenting-casing\"><h4>Fragmenting Casing</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Consumable</p><p>A bomb gains 10 feet additional splash radius and +3 × Core Tier splash damage. Allies in the enlarged area are affected normally; do not multiply direct-hit damage.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Pyroceramics · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 1 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-3-shaped-charge\"><h4>Shaped Charge</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Consumable</p><p>On use choose concentrated detonation: remove all splash damage and add Core Tier d12 primary damage against the directly hit creature or object. A miss does not deal this additional damage.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Pyroceramics · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 1 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-3-pressure-vessel\"><h4>Pressure Vessel</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Consumable</p><p>Multiply the explosive&#39;s base primary damage dice by 3. Do not multiply flat bonuses, splash, persistent damage or added Mark dice. A critical manufacturing failure destroys the paid ordinary casing inputs.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Pyroceramics · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 2 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-3-furnace-heart\"><h4>Furnace Heart</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 2 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Two actions, once per day: a 20-foot emanation deals 3 × Core Tier d8 fire damage to other creatures, basic Reflex against your higher class/spell DC. The item also serves as a portable forge for downtime when set down safely.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Pyroceramics · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 2 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00019","name":"Weaving — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1900000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Weaving — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>High-power campaign revision: all 253 Marks have been reviewed. Flat Artisan bonuses stack; resistances use the highest applicable source. Capacity and the one-free-Mark limit still apply.</p><p>Campaign descriptions are not a promise that every effect is automated. Supported passive numbers use the item rules; activations, auras, project changes and special riders require manual resolution unless stated otherwise. Native action readouts do not spend uses automatically. Structure Marks never grant character bonuses.</p><p>Where a Mark grants a separate 10-point temporary-HP buffer, track it alongside class temporary HP. Spend the Artisan buffer first, then ordinary temporary HP, then HP. Different Mark buffers may coexist; the same grant cannot refill through re-equipping and expires as written. Maximum-HP increases are not healing.</p><h2>Universal Artisan Marks</h2><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-universal-lightweave\"><h4>Lightweave</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Reduce this primarily textile item&#39;s Bulk by 2, minimum 0. This does not reduce the Bulk of its contents or other carried equipment.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-universal-perfect-thread\"><h4>Perfect Thread</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Project</p><p>Gain +Core Tier + 2 on the next Tailoring or Leatherwork project check that consumes this textile. Once consumed, the thread cannot grant this benefit to a second project.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-universal-reinforced-weave\"><h4>Slipknot Weave</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to Athletics and Acrobatics checks to Escape, not unarmed Escape attacks.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-universal-weatherproof-weave\"><h4>Weatherproof Weave</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor ignores ordinary rain exposure and grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Fortitude saves against severe non-magical weather. Enable the Mark condition only for weather.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-universal-tensioned-thread\"><h4>Tensioned Thread</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>A woven weapon gains +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Athletics checks to Grapple or Trip with it. Enable the Mark condition only when using that weapon, and it must already have the relevant trait.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Aetherweaving</h2><p>Manathread and magical cloth that carry enchantments, wards, and arcane patterns.</p><h3>Signature — Manathread</h3><p>Produce magically conductive fabric capable of storing, carrying and shaping supernatural energy.</p><h3>Mastery — Arcane Loom</h3><p>Weave stronger magical fibres and exotic feedstocks without losing their properties.</p><h3>Legacy — Magical Textile Industry</h3><p>Supports magical garments, banners, specialist exports and arcane infrastructure.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-1-resonant-thread\"><h4>Resonant Thread</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Project</p><p>Textile supplies mana, conductor and aetherwoven tags for compatible work. Its visible pattern grants +Core Tier + 2 to identify its own magic; it does not add free Marks or spell slots.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Aetherweaving · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-1-manaweave\"><h4>Manaweave</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants resistance equal to 4 × Core Tier to one chosen acid, cold, electricity or fire type. Use the highest applicable resistance source.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Aetherweaving · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-1-spellthread\"><h4>Spellthread</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · 2 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Two actions once per day: restore 6 × Core Tier HP to one willing touched creature and let it immediately Step up to 10 feet. This is a magical restoration activation, not a stored spell slot.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Aetherweaving · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-1-ethereal-weave\"><h4>Ethereal Weave</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Free Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Ignore non-magical ground difficult terrain while wearing this armor. Free action once per encounter: Step up to 20 feet through occupied creature spaces, ending in an open space. Does not pass through walls.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Aetherweaving · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-1-expanded-matrix\"><h4>Expanded Matrix</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Project</p><p>Reduce the Capacity cost of one compatible paid Enchanting or Tailoring Mark by 2, minimum 1. Total costs still cannot exceed Core Capacity. Discounts apply to the original cost, not recursively.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Aetherweaving · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 2 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-1-aetherbound-form\"><h4>Aetherbound Form</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 2 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Two actions once per day for 1 minute: gain fly Speed 40 feet, physical resistance equal to 5 × Core Tier, and squeeze through openings as though two sizes smaller. You are not incorporeal and cannot pass through solid walls.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Aetherweaving · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 2 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Ironweaving</h2><p>Warcloth, armour backing, nets, ropes, bowstrings, sails, and resilient reinforcement.</p><h3>Signature — Warcloth</h3><p>Produce armour backing, nets, ropes, strings, sails and flexible reinforcement designed for combat stress.</p><h3>Mastery — Steel Thread</h3><p>Integrate stronger materials without sacrificing flexibility.</p><h3>Legacy — Military Textiles</h3><p>Supports armour, siege gear, sails, ropes and army equipment.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-2-warcloth-finish\"><h4>Warcloth Finish</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Textile armor gains +100% of pre-Mark maximum item HP. This does not increase wearer HP; other durability bonuses use the same original base.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Ironweaving · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-2-impact-mesh\"><h4>Impact Mesh</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · 2 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants physical resistance equal to 3 × Core Tier. Resistance does not add to other physical-resistance sources. Impact Lock — Two actions, once per encounter: until the start of your next turn, increase this Mark&#39;s physical resistance to 6 × Core Tier. This replaces its passive resistance for that duration; do not add the two together. Resolve the temporary increase manually.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Ironweaving · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-2-flexible-weave\"><h4>Flexible Weave</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Reduce this armor&#39;s land Speed penalty by 15 feet, minimum 0, and raise its Dexterity modifier cap by 3. This changes the armor cap, not your Dexterity score.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Ironweaving · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-2-shock-absorbing-warcloth\"><h4>Shock-Absorbing Warcloth</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants +12 × Core Tier maximum HP. This replaces per-turn temporary HP; it does not heal when equipped or grant damage absorption beyond the maximum-HP increase.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Ironweaving · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-2-silken-steel\"><h4>Silken Steel</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants +5 Artisan Bonus to AC beyond Core progression and physical resistance equal to 4 × Core Tier. AC stacks with different Marks; resistance uses the highest source.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Ironweaving · Core Tier 4+; Core-tier Anchor required</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 2 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-2-unbreakable-braid\"><h4>Lifeline Braid</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants bleed resistance equal to 5 × Core Tier and an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to Athletics and Acrobatics checks to Escape, not unarmed Escape attacks.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Ironweaving · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 2 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Heraldweaving</h2><p>Standards, banners, and tapestries supporting morale, identity, armies, and prestige.</p><h3>Signature — Great Standards</h3><p>Create banners and tapestries that carry morale, identity and supernatural command presence.</p><h3>Mastery — Living Heraldry</h3><p>Standards grow more potent when tied to a recognised army, ruler, settlement or company.</p><h3>Legacy — National Identity</h3><p>Supports armies, festivals, loyalty, diplomacy and prestige.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-3-heraldic-seal\"><h4>Heraldic Seal</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Society checks proving the authority or affiliation displayed by this worn armor. Enable the Mark condition only where that affiliation matters.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Heraldweaving · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-3-unbroken-standard\"><h4>Unbroken Standard</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>While this focus is held and displayed, allies within 30 feet who can see it gain +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to saves against fear. The bearer must be conscious; resolve recipients manually.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Heraldweaving · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-3-marching-banner\"><h4>Marching Banner</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Allies starting their turns within 30 feet of the displayed focus gain +15 feet Artisan land Speed for that turn and ignore the first 15 feet of difficult terrain. Does not grant extra actions.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Heraldweaving · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-3-kings-colours\"><h4>King&#39;s Colours</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Allies within 30 feet of the displayed focus gain +5 Artisan Bonus to Aid checks and saves against mental effects while they can see its conscious bearer.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Heraldweaving · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-3-conquerors-standard\"><h4>Conqueror&#39;s Standard</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 2 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Two actions once per encounter for 1 minute: when an ally within 30 feet reduces a hostile creature to 0 HP, that ally gains +5 Artisan Bonus to attacks until the end of its next turn. Multiple defeats refresh duration, not bonus magnitude.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Heraldweaving · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 2 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-3-sovereign-standard\"><h4>Sovereign Standard</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 2 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Two actions once per day for 1 minute: allies within 30 feet gain +5 Artisan Bonus to saves and +3 × Core Tier damage on their first hit each round. On activation grant each ally a separately tracked 10-point Artisan temporary-HP buffer, expiring after 1 minute. Do not overwrite class temporary HP; record and deduct the buffer manually.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Heraldweaving · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 2 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00020","name":"Bookmaking — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":2000000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Bookmaking — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>High-power campaign revision: all 253 Marks have been reviewed. Flat Artisan bonuses stack; resistances use the highest applicable source. Capacity and the one-free-Mark limit still apply.</p><p>Campaign descriptions are not a promise that every effect is automated. Supported passive numbers use the item rules; activations, auras, project changes and special riders require manual resolution unless stated otherwise. Native action readouts do not spend uses automatically. Structure Marks never grant character bonuses.</p><p>Where a Mark grants a separate 10-point temporary-HP buffer, track it alongside class temporary HP. Spend the Artisan buffer first, then ordinary temporary HP, then HP. Different Mark buffers may coexist; the same grant cannot refill through re-equipping and expires as written. Maximum-HP increases are not healing.</p><h2>Universal Artisan Marks</h2><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-universal-perfect-index\"><h4>Perfect Index</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Find any recorded entry in this held focus immediately. Gain +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Society checks to Recall Knowledge directly documented in it; enable the Mark condition only for that subject.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-universal-preserved-knowledge\"><h4>Preserved Knowledge</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>The work is immune to mundane water, ageing and mildew. A legible copy of damaged pages can be restored during one hour of study if at least half the original survives; it does not recover erased magical secrets.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-universal-master-copy\"><h4>Master Copy</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Project</p><p>Copy a paid formula or mundane text in one-quarter normal downtime, minimum 10 minutes. Material and licence costs remain; copying does not duplicate magic, consumables or activation charges.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 1 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-universal-encoded-script\"><h4>Encoded Script</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Gain +Core Tier + 2 to the DC to Decipher Writing in this focus without its key. Authorised readers can read normally; possession of a stolen key bypasses the encoding.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 1 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-universal-reference-tabs\"><h4>Reference Tabs</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Free Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Free action once per 10 minutes before Recall Knowledge using this held focus&#39;s recorded subject: gain +5 Artisan Bonus to that check. No benefit on an undocumented subject.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 1 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Grimoirecraft</h2><p>Living spellbooks and codices with enhanced memory, resonance, organisation, and access.</p><h3>Signature — Living Grimoires</h3><p>Create spellbooks and codices that interact directly with spell preparation, memory and magical resonance.</p><h3>Mastery — Arcane Codex</h3><p>Improve magical capacity, indexing and stability while reducing time to expand or revise the grimoire.</p><h3>Legacy — Grand Academies</h3><p>Supports magical education, spell research and institutional knowledge.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-1-indexed-arcana\"><h4>Indexed Arcana</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Held focus grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Arcana checks about spells recorded in it. Enable the Mark condition only for those spells; the index locates their entries immediately.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-1-mnemonic-pages\"><h4>Mnemonic Pages</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Once per day after 10 minutes of study, replace up to three unexpended prepared spells with known spells of the same ranks. Does not restore spent slots or grant spells the reader cannot normally prepare.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 1 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-1-resonant-chapter\"><h4>Resonant Chapter</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Choose one spell trait at creation. Spells with that trait gain +3 damage per spell rank on their first damage roll against each target. This is flat bonus damage, not multiplied ongoing damage; record the chosen trait.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 1 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-1-spell-echo\"><h4>Spell Echo</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Reaction</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Reaction once per encounter after a spell deals damage to one target: deal additional damage equal to Core Tier d8 of its primary type to that target or a second creature within 15 feet. Basic Reflex against your spell DC. This is a separate magical echo and cannot echo itself.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 1 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-1-archmage-codex\"><h4>Archmage Codex</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 2 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Elemental Thesis — Choose Acid, Cold, Electricity, Fire or Sonic when applying this Mark. While holding this spell focus, damaging spells bearing the chosen elemental trait gain bonus damage of that type. Passive formula: 2 × spell damage die (3 × at Core Tier 6). Ascendant Thesis — Two actions, once per encounter for 1 minute: replace the passive bonus with (Core Tier + 2) × spell damage die. Use the chosen type&#39;s first base damage component and its largest die; if that type is absent, use the spell&#39;s first base component. Flat-only components provide no bonus dice. Example: Core Tier 4 with a d6 spell adds 2d6 passively or 6d6 while activated. Add this once to initial damage, not each missile, persistent tick or later repeated damage. Enable Initial Spell Damage only for that roll. Enable Ascendant Thesis after activation and clear it when the minute ends. Uses and duration are tracked manually; active and passive dice never add together.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 2 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-1-endless-grimoire\"><h4>Endless Grimoire</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 3 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Three actions once per day: recover one expended spell slot of rank no higher than Core Tier, maximum 6. It cannot recover a slot used to create permanent resources, restore slots or activate another recovery effect. Non-slot casters require a recorded equivalent before crafting.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 2 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Chroniclecraft</h2><p>Lore, formulae, techniques, and Codices of Mastery that make recorded knowledge usable.</p><h3>Signature — Codices of Mastery</h3><p>Record Lore, formulae, techniques and expertise precisely enough that others can temporarily benefit from it.</p><h3>Mastery — Perfect Instruction</h3><p>Preserve increasingly advanced knowledge while reducing training/research time.</p><h3>Legacy — Great Library</h3><p>Improves research, education, formula preservation and Culture.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-2-scholars-index\"><h4>Scholar&#39;s Index</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Held focus grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Society research checks on its documented subject. Enable the Mark condition only during that research.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-2-lore-codex\"><h4>Lore Codex</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>After 10 minutes study choose one recorded narrow Lore. Gain +5 Artisan Bonus to checks with that Lore for 8 hours, even if untrained, but do not gain proficiency ranks or trained-only actions.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 1 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-2-crafting-manual\"><h4>Crafting Manual</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Project</p><p>For one recorded recipe family reduce required artisan-days by 40%, minimum one, and gain +5 to its first project check each day. Reductions use original work; this does not create free materials.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 1 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-2-tactical-treatise\"><h4>Tactical Treatise</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Free Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Free action once per encounter before an attack, save or Recall Knowledge against a documented creature trait: gain +5 Artisan Bonus to that roll. The trait is chosen at creation and must match the target.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 1 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-2-masters-testament\"><h4>Master&#39;s Testament</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>During daily preparations choose one of three recorded skill feats whose level and other prerequisites you meet. Gain its use until next preparations. No ancestry, class, dedication or spellcasting feats; it cannot grant crafting outputs retroactively.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 2 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-2-legendary-chronicle\"><h4>Legendary Chronicle</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Up to six readers study for 10 minutes during daily preparations. Each gains +5 Artisan Bonus to one recorded narrow Lore for the day and one fortune reroll of a failed check with that Lore, using the new result. Restudying does not reset uses.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 2 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Grand Cartography</h2><p>Master atlases for exploration, resources, roads, armies, settlements, and expansion.</p><h3>Signature — Master Atlas</h3><p>Create maps that record resources, hazards, routes, magical phenomena and strategic terrain.</p><h3>Mastery — Perfect Survey</h3><p>Reveal hidden resources and improve route accuracy with less exploration time.</p><h3>Legacy — Kingdom Survey</h3><p>Improves hex claims, roads, army movement, settlement placement and resource exploitation.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-3-surveyors-mark\"><h4>Surveyor&#39;s Mark</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Held map grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Survival checks to navigate its recorded territory. Enable the Mark condition only within mapped territory.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Grand Cartography · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-3-safe-passage\"><h4>Safe Passage</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Project</p><p>In mapped territory reduce travel delays from documented non-magical hazards by 50%. Does not increase encounter Speed, remove hazards outright or reduce an undelayed journey.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Grand Cartography · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 1 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-3-resource-survey\"><h4>Resource Survey</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Project</p><p>A successful survey reveals one hidden ordinary resource site and grants +5 on the first extraction check there each Kingdom turn. No resource is created without a site; unique discoveries remain GM-controlled.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Grand Cartography · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 1 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-3-strategic-map\"><h4>Strategic Map</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Held map grants +5 Artisan Bonus to initiative in its recorded region when studied for 10 minutes earlier that day. Enable the Mark condition only within the studied region.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Grand Cartography · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 1 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-3-hidden-paths\"><h4>Hidden Paths</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Project</p><p>Establish a mapped secret route: travel along it takes half normal non-combat time and travellers gain +5 to avoid detection on the route. It cannot cross impassable terrain or ignore hostile fortifications.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Grand Cartography · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 2 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-3-world-atlas\"><h4>World Atlas</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Project</p><p>At each Kingdom turn choose one mapped region: double ordinary resource output, halve ordinary travel time, or gain +5 on settlement-planning checks there for that turn. Only one mode applies; never duplicate unique or story resources.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Grand Cartography · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 2 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00021","name":"Tailoring — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":2100000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Tailoring — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>High-power campaign revision: all 253 Marks have been reviewed. Flat Artisan bonuses stack; resistances use the highest applicable source. Capacity and the one-free-Mark limit still apply.</p><p>Campaign descriptions are not a promise that every effect is automated. Supported passive numbers use the item rules; activations, auras, project changes and special riders require manual resolution unless stated otherwise. Native action readouts do not spend uses automatically. Structure Marks never grant character bonuses.</p><p>Where a Mark grants a separate 10-point temporary-HP buffer, track it alongside class temporary HP. Spend the Artisan buffer first, then ordinary temporary HP, then HP. Different Mark buffers may coexist; the same grant cannot refill through re-equipping and expires as written. Maximum-HP increases are not healing.</p><h2>Universal Artisan Marks</h2><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-universal-perfect-fit\"><h4>Tailored First Impression</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier + 2 to Diplomacy checks to Make an Impression. This does not compel agreement or bypass attitudes.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-universal-reinforced-seam\"><h4>Steadfast Hem</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants an Artisan Bonus equal to Core Tier to Will saves against fear. Enable the Mark condition only against fear effects.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-universal-hidden-pocketing\"><h4>Hidden Pocketing</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Thievery checks to Conceal an Object in its fitted pockets. Enable the Mark condition only for an object that fits; Bulk is unchanged.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-universal-quick-access-cut\"><h4>Quick-Access Cut</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Once per round draw one accessible light object as part of the action that uses it. Also secure two additional light objects against accidental loss. Does not reduce the use action&#39;s cost.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-universal-layered-lining\"><h4>Layered Lining</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Project</p><p>Garment supports two paid secondary textile or leather components without additional empty-lining Bulk. Materials and Marks still cost normally; this grants no Capacity or duplicate Core progression.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Battlestitching</h2><p>Combat garments and armour liners designed for movement, access, protection, and adaptation.</p><h3>Signature — War Garments</h3><p>Create combat robes, coats, armour liners, harnesses and flexible protection.</p><h3>Mastery — Combat Cut</h3><p>Increase protection without sacrificing movement and reduce material waste when refitting worn gear.</p><h3>Legacy — Military Tailoring</h3><p>Supports elite uniforms, armour liners and specialised army equipment.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-1-combat-cut\"><h4>Combat Cut</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Acrobatics checks to Tumble Through. It does not change movement cost or negate reactions from a failed check.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Battlestitching · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-1-quickdraw-harness\"><h4>Quickdraw Harness</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Free Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Free action once per round: draw up to two weapons secured to this harness, provided you have enough free hands. It does not make a Strike or reduce other activation costs.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Battlestitching · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-1-vital-reinforcement\"><h4>Vital Reinforcement</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants +18 × Core Tier maximum HP. This is maximum HP, not temporary HP or healing; repeated equipping must not restore damage.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Battlestitching · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-1-reactive-weave\"><h4>Reactive Weave</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Reaction</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Reaction once per round when damaged: reduce that damage instance by 6 × Core Tier, or 10 × Core Tier if caused by a critical hit, minimum 0. This is reduction of one instance, not resistance for the round.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Battlestitching · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-1-war-skin\"><h4>Duelist&#39;s War-Skin</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants Artisan Bonuses of Core Tier to AC and Reflex saves, and 5 × Core Tier feet to land Speed. It grants no physical resistance.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Battlestitching · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 2 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-1-war-skin-regeneration\"><h4>War-Skin Regeneration</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants +24 × Core Tier maximum HP. Once per day after an encounter, spend 10 minutes adjusting it to restore 8 × Core Tier HP. Replaces per-turn temporary HP and cannot heal through repeated equipping.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Battlestitching · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 2 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Veilcraft</h2><p>Supernatural disguises, stealth clothing, concealing mantles, and perception-altering garments.</p><h3>Signature — Impossible Garments</h3><p>Manipulate sight, sound, shadow, identity and supernatural concealment through clothing.</p><h3>Mastery — Perfect Veil</h3><p>Improve disguise/concealment reliability and reduce the signs left by supernatural garments.</p><h3>Legacy — Shadow Service</h3><p>Supports scouts, spies, diplomats and intelligence networks.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-2-silent-stitch\"><h4>Silent Stitch</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Stealth checks where clothing noise matters. Enable the Mark condition only when muffling the garment would help.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Veilcraft · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-2-chameleon-cloth\"><h4>Chameleon Cloth</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Stealth checks to Hide or Sneak in one recorded environment palette. Enable the Mark condition only there; no half-Speed requirement beyond normal Sneak rules.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Veilcraft · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-2-many-faced-weave\"><h4>Many-Faced Weave</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>One minute of adjustment creates a recorded mundane disguise of clothing and facial framing. Gain +5 Artisan Bonus to Deception checks to Impersonate that identity. No size change or copied abilities; close examination still permits detection.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Veilcraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-2-shadow-mantle\"><h4>Shadow Mantle</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · 1 Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>One action once per encounter for 1 minute: gain concealed in dim light or darkness and +Core Tier Artisan Bonus to Stealth there. Attacking does not end concealment, but bright light suppresses it until you leave that light.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Veilcraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-2-phase-veil\"><h4>Phase Veil</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 1 Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>One action once per encounter until the end of your next turn: move through creature spaces and non-magical difficult terrain, gaining physical resistance equal to 6 × Core Tier. You cannot cross solid walls and must end movement in open space.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Veilcraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 2 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-2-null-mantle\"><h4>Null Mantle</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 1 Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>One action once per day for 1 minute: become invisible and gain +5 Artisan Bonus to saves against magical detection. Hostile actions suppress invisibility until the start of your next turn. Does not negate precise non-visual senses.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Veilcraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 2 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Regaliacraft</h2><p>Vestments of authority supporting diplomacy, leadership, morale, royal courts, and prestige.</p><h3>Signature — Vestments of Authority</h3><p>Create royal, diplomatic, ceremonial and command garments that reinforce office and presence.</p><h3>Mastery — Perfect Regalia</h3><p>Regalia becomes stronger when properly tied to a recognised office, ruler or institution.</p><h3>Legacy — Royal Court</h3><p>Improves diplomacy, loyalty, leadership, festivals, prestige and foreign relations.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-3-court-finish\"><h4>Court Finish</h4><p><strong>Minor · 0 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Society checks involving formal protocol or heraldry. Enable the Mark condition only for those subjects.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Regaliacraft · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-3-envoys-raiment\"><h4>Envoy&#39;s Raiment</h4><p><strong>Standard · 1 Capacity · Free Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants +Core Tier + 2 Artisan Bonus to Diplomacy checks when acting in an officially recognised capacity. Enable the Mark condition only with a relevant mandate; social consequences still apply. Envoy&#39;s Reprise — Free action, once per day after failing a Diplomacy check made in your recognised official capacity: reroll and use the new result. This is a fortune effect; it cannot combine with another fortune effect on that roll.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Regaliacraft · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-3-commanders-mantle\"><h4>Commander&#39;s Mantle</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · Passive</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Conscious wearer visibly leading allies grants those allies within 30 feet +5 Artisan Bonus to Aid checks and saves against fear. The wearer is not their own ally for this aura; record recipients manually.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Regaliacraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-3-judicators-robes\"><h4>Judicator&#39;s Robes</h4><p><strong>Major · 2 Capacity · 1 Action</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · Item</p><p>Gain +5 Artisan Bonus to Perception checks to Sense Motive. One action once per encounter: designate a visible creature within 60 feet; allies gain +5 Artisan Bonus to their first save against it before the end of your next turn.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Regaliacraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-3-sovereign-presence\"><h4>Sovereign Presence</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 2 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Two actions once per encounter for 1 minute: allies within 30 feet gain +5 Artisan Bonus to saves. Enemies within 30 feet take -3 Artisan Bonus to saves against your fear effects. This is a mental aura; unconsciousness ends it.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Regaliacraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 2 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-3-coronation-regalia\"><h4>Coronation Regalia</h4><p><strong>Superior · 3 Capacity · 2 Actions</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · Item</p><p>Worn armor grants its recognised office-holder +18 × Core Tier maximum HP and +5 Artisan Bonus to Diplomacy and Intimidation. Two actions once per day: allies within 30 feet gain a separately tracked 10-point Artisan temporary-HP buffer for 10 minutes. Do not overwrite class temporary HP; track and deduct this buffer manually.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Regaliacraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 2 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div></section>"}}]}
